R1149,TRADING ATHLETES: THE UNREGULATED MARKET of INDIAN FANTASY PLAYER STOCKS,"This article examines the regulatory challenges posed by Fantasy Player Stock Trading (FPST) platforms in India, which uniquely blend gaming and financial market mechanics. Unlike traditional fantasy sports, FPST platforms utilize sophisticated trading features, including algorithmic pricing, leveraged positions, and market-driven price discovery. This analysis demonstrates that current gaming regulations and self-regulatory mechanisms are inadequate to address the inherent complexities of FPSTs, which operate like unregulated securities markets. Although FPST tokens do not neatly fit the legal definition of “securities,” their functional equivalence with financial markets, coupled with their addictive design and systemic vulnerabilities, necessitates a bespoke regulatory framework and oversight. This article underlines the necessity of immediate regulatory attention to protect gamers, advocating for a new regulatory approach beyond existing gambling or gaming parameters.",2026,Sharma,Gaming Law Review,10.1177/25725300261420625,,https://doi.org/10.1177/25725300261420625,en,openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1150,At the Crossroads: Sports Betting in Missouri and Proposals for Regulations,"Sports betting is a rapidly growing industry nationwide, and Missouri became the 39th state to legalize the practice. Although states hope to reap the benefits of a regulated sports gambling market, the activity carries significant mental, physical, and socioeconomic risks due to its inherently addictive nature. The hyper-accessibility of modern platforms, particularly those enabling unlimited micro betting, magnifies longstanding concerns in a new digital context. Compounding these risks, the absence of federal standards for minimum wagering ages and the aggressive marketing strategies employed by sportsbooks draw in young adults. This article proposes a coordinated federal and state regulatory framework that would establish a minimum wagering age, constrain sportsbooks’ marketing practices, and limit micro-betting options to better protect consumers in Missouri.",2026,Shumate,bepress Legal Repository,,,,,openalex:article,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1151,"ANALYZING THE DETERMINANTS, PSYCHOLOGICAL CORRELATES, AND INTERVENTION STRATEGIES FOR ONLINE GAMING ADDICTION AMONG AVIATOR BET USERS IN NAIROBI COUNTY, KENYA","The rapid proliferation of digital gaming and betting platforms has fundamentally transformed patterns of leisure, economic participation, and behavioral health across the globe, with particularly acute implications for emerging digital economies in sub-Saharan Africa. The small but growing niche occupied by hybridal types of gaming-gambling games, like the Aviator Bet service, has combined real-time wagering systems with the high frequency nature of gaming in ways that increase the susceptibility to compulsive and addictive behavior. The overlap of efforts to provide a mobile financial infrastructure, most prominently M-Pesa, and a greater Sony number of more advanced online betting technologies has provided a space in which younger adult online gambling addicts are uniquely predisposed to form behavioral addiction patterns. The paper explores the predictors, mental factors, and treatment consequences of online gaming addiction between the users of Aviator Bet in the Nairobi County, Kenya with the two-fold aim of defining the extent of the issue, and analyzing evidence-based interventions.To obtain convergent qualitative and quantitative data, a parallel mixed-methods approach was used that combined quantitative survey data that was gathered on 248 participants who are adults and qualitative information obtained via the in-depth interview. The study sample was selected using stratified sampling in the different sub-counties in Nairobi, which is a diverse city and peri-urban area. The high prevalence of moderate to severe online gaming addiction was found as quantitative results, where 62.5% of the participants fit the criteria of engaging in a way that was considered to be clinically significant. Regression analysis proved the severity of addiction as a significant predictor of psychological distress (0.48, p &lt;.001) and significant positive correlation was identified between addiction severity and anxiety (r =.52), depression (r =.49) and perceived stress (r =.46). Social outcomes were also evident with high addiction levels showing the existence of financial strain ( 0.41, p &lt;.01), interpersonal conflict ( ${-0.37, p &lt;.01).It is the qualitative data that complemented these quantitative trends by pointing to cognitive distortions such as illusions of control and gamblertype fallacy thinking, maladaptive coping styles, vulnerability of socioeconomic status and peer normalization as primary psychosocial influences in perpetuating and maintaining compulsive involvement.",2026,SIGEI,International Journal of Social Sciences and Management Review,10.37602/ijssmr.2026.9320,,https://doi.org/10.37602/ijssmr.2026.9320,und,openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle;Review,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1152,WHEN LEGALIZATION PRECEDES REGULATION: REGULATORY TIMING AND THE DEVELOPMENT OF SPORTS BETTING MARKETS,"Governments increasingly face the challenge of regulating newly legalized markets while simultaneously protecting consumers and mitigating social harms. While existing research has focused primarily on the design of regulatory instruments, comparatively little attention has been devoted to the consequences of delaying regulation after legalization. This article develops a regulatory sequencing perspective to examine how the timing of regulation may influence market development and consumer behavior. Drawing on the legalization of fixed-odds sports betting in Brazil, where a comprehensive regulatory framework was implemented several years after legalization, this article argues that delayed regulation shaped the market environment policymakers inherited. It identifies three mechanisms through which this occurred: the normalization of betting and the diffusion of consumer beliefs before the implementation of effective consumer protection measures; the widespread adoption of high-engagement product and platform design features in the absence of regulatory constraints; and the reduced capacity of regulatory institutions to influence market dynamics after commercial practices and industry structures had become established. Rather than treating regulatory timing as a procedural detail, this article argues that it constitutes an important determinant of policy effectiveness in newly legalized markets. Beyond the Brazilian case, the analysis contributes to broader debates on gambling regulation by highlighting how the sequencing of legalization and regulation can shape both market trajectories and the effectiveness of subsequent regulatory intervention.",2026,Sigrist,Gaming Law Review,10.1177/25725300261487889,,https://doi.org/10.1177/25725300261487889,en,crossref:journal-article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;crossref,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1153,"Understanding the Socio-Demographic Profiles and Motivations behind Youth Participation in Sports Betting: A case study of Dar es Salaam City, Tanzania","This study examines the socio-demographic profiles and motivations of youth sports bettors in Dar es Salaam city, Tanzania. The study employed a cross-sectional design; data were collected from 205 participants across five wards through mixed-methods analysis. Both primary and secondary data were used in this study, while the data analysis involved SPSS. The study is anchored in Rational Choice Theory, Social Learning Theory and Sustainable Livelihood Frameworks; challenging the ""idleness"" myth, and suggesting that sports betting is a rational, albeit high-risk, adaptive strategy to structural economic constraints and urban income instability. Findings reveal that betting participation is not limited only to marginalized youth. While economic gain serves as the primary driver; social environments play a critical role in sustaining betting practices. The study concludes that social learning in urban hubs (vijiwe) sustains participation beyond initial entry. Recommendations include implementing stricter zoning regulations for betting outlets near residential areas and developing community-based programs that offer more stable financial growth than speculative gambling. This research emphasizes shifting policy from moralistic discouragement toward evidence-based structural interventions beyond Dar es Salaam context.",2026,Silayo,Tanzania Journal of Community Development,10.4314/tajocode.v5i1.6,,https://doi.org/10.4314/tajocode.v5i1.6,und,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R1154,"Implementing Lower Latency, Fast Startup and Switching for low-latency low-delay (L3D) DASH","Low-latency video streaming is essential for interactive applications such as sports betting and live concerts. The sixth edition of the MPEG DASH specification introduces new features enabling the L3D-DASH (Low Latency, Low Delay DASH) approach, which aims to minimize startup times and playback latencies. This paper presents an overview of L3D-DASH and details its implementation on the encoder and packager side, as well as on the client-side. We describe the encoding and packaging pipeline optimized for ultra-low-latency, including parallel video streams with distinct IDR placement strategies and the use of the Live Media Ingest protocol for efficient media delivery. On the client side, we discuss the implementation in dash.js and the challenges of L3D-DASH, such as adaptive bitrate switching and precise playback start and seeking. We then compare the performance of L3D DASH against classic non low latency DASH content. Initial results demonstrate that L3D-DASH achieves faster startup and a more stable low latency playback compared to classic DASH content. These findings highlight the potential of L3D-DASH to advance the state of low-latency streaming and improve user experience in latency-sensitive scenarios.",2026,Silhavy,Mile-High Video Conference (MHV),10.1145/3789239.3793277,,https://doi.org/10.1145/3789239.3793277,en,datacite:Other/conference paper | openaire:Article; Conference object | openalex:conference-paper | openalex:other | s2:JournalArticle;Book;Review,openalex;s2;datacite;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R1156,A REGULAMENTAÇÃO DAS APOSTAS ESPORTIVAS E O RISCO DE MANIPULAÇÃO DE PARTIDAS DE FUTEBOL NO BRASIL,"A significativa ampliação do número de apostas esportivas no Brasil, ocasionada pelas plataformas digitais, tem revelado riscos à integridade das competições e à segurança da atividade. A possibilidade de manipulação em partidas de futebol e a atuação de organizações criminosas expõem fragilidades no atual modelo regulatório. Portanto, este estudo tem por objetivo analisar os desafios jurídicos e institucionais atinentes à regulação da atividade de apostas esportivas no Brasil, considerando, sobretudo, os riscos concretos de manipulação de resultados e corrupção desportiva. A metodologia adotada é de natureza qualitativa, exploratória e teórico-dogmática, com base em análise bibliográfica. Os resultados indicam a existência de um arcabouço normativo incipiente, marcado pela ausência de tipificação penal específica, pela fragilidade institucional na fiscalização das casas de apostas e pela carência de integração entre os órgãos reguladores. Verificou-se que os mecanismos atuais de repressão são insuficientes para enfrentar supostos esquemas de manipulação de resultados, exigindo um modelo de governança mais estruturado, preventivo e aparelhado. Também foi possível constatar a necessidade de adoção de medidas como educação preventiva, auditorias, compliance esportivo e cooperação internacional. Conclui-se que a regulamentação das apostas esportivas depende da articulação entre legislação, fiscalização e políticas públicas integradas, a fim de proteger a integridade do esporte e a confiança da sociedade no sistema.",2026,Silva,Revista Tópicos.,10.70773/revistatopicos/784328851,,https://doi.org/10.70773/revistatopicos/784328851,und,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en;crossref;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1157,A RELAÇÃO ENTRE AS APOSTAS ESPORTIVAS DIGITAIS E A FRAGILIDADE DA EDUCAÇÃO FINANCEIRA NO BRASIL,"O crescimento das apostas esportivas digitais no Brasil tem chamado cada vez mais a atenção devido aos seus impactos econômicos e comportamentais, especialmente entre jovens e pessoas em situação de vulnerabilidade financeira. Nesse contexto, este estudo analisa a relação entre a expansão das apostas esportivas, a educação financeira e as condições socioeconômicas da população brasileira. Para isso, foi realizada uma pesquisa qualitativa de caráter bibliográfico e documental, baseada na análise de artigos científicos, relatórios institucionais e dados oficiais publicados entre 2020 e 2025. Os resultados indicam que a popularização das apostas está relacionada à facilidade de acesso às plataformas digitais, à intensa exposição publicitária e à busca por ganhos imediatos. Também foi observado que estados com menor renda média e maior dependência de programas de auxílio governamental de renda apresentam maior participação em apostas esportivas, sugerindo relação entre vulnerabilidade econômica e comportamentos financeiros de risco. Conclui-se que o avanço das apostas esportivas digitais está associado a fatores econômicos, sociais e comportamentais, reforçando a importância da educação financeira e de políticas públicas voltadas à conscientização e à prevenção do endividamento. Além disso, o tema demanda atenção crescente por parte da sociedade e da comunidade acadêmica. Para pesquisas futuras, recomenda-se a realização de estudos empíricos sobre os impactos das apostas nas finanças pessoais, na saúde mental e no comportamento dos indivíduos.",2026,Silva,Revista de Geopolítica,10.56238/revgeov17n7-100,,https://doi.org/10.56238/revgeov17n7-100,und,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en;crossref;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1158,CENTRAL DE REGULAÇÃO DE VAGAS E RESPONSABILIDADE SISTÊMICA: UMA CRÍTICA À TRANSFERÊNCIA DO ÔNUS ESTRUTURAL DA SUPERLOTAÇÃO PRISIONAL AO PODER JUDICIÁRIO,"O artigo analisa criticamente a Central de Regulação de Vagas (CRV), metodologia desenvolvida pelo Conselho Nacional de Justiça (CNJ) para enfrentar a superlotação do sistema prisional brasileiro. Sustenta-se que a CRV incorre em equívoco estrutural ao atribuir ao Judiciário o encargo de compensar omissões historicamente imputáveis ao Poder Legislativo — pelo progressivo endurecimento da política criminal sem correspondente provisão de vagas, tendência intensificada no biênio 2025-2026 — e ao Poder Executivo — pela insuficiência crônica de investimento em infraestrutura penitenciária e pelo redirecionamento de recursos das apostas esportivas para finalidades alheias à criação de vagas. O artigo reconhece a parcela de responsabilidade do Judiciário — especialmente pela manutenção de prisões preventivas além do prazo razoável e pelo represamento de progressões de regime — e aponta as contradições internas do próprio Poder Judiciário, que cobra da magistratura ordinária o combate à superlotação enquanto profere decisões com impacto expansivo sobre a população carcerária. O Amazonas é apresentado como estudo de caso paradigmático: estado com a segunda menor taxa de aprisionamento do país (166,10 por 100 mil habitantes), não por eficiência do sistema, mas por ausência estrutural de vagas, assolado por disputas faccionais desde 2016 e palco de dois massacres em unidades superlotadas (2017 e 2019). O fenômeno resultante é denominado ativismo judicial compulsório por omissão alheia: o juiz é responsabilizado por gerir o que décadas de inação executiva e legislativa não construíram. Ao final, propõem-se soluções de distribuição constitucionalmente adequada de responsabilidades entre os três Poderes.",2026,Silva,Derecho y cambio social.,10.54899/dcs.v23i97.7325,,https://doi.org/10.54899/dcs.v23i97.7325,,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1163,"Mulheres nas apostas esportivas no Brasil: crescimento, perfil e fatores determinantes em 2025","O presente estudo analisa o crescimento da participação feminina no mercado de apostas esportivas no Brasil, que atingiu 37% em 2025. O objetivo é compreender os fatores que impulsionam esse aumento, bem como identificar diferenças comportamentais em relação ao público masculino. A metodologia adotada foi de caráter exploratório, com base em dados secundários provenientes de relatórios de mercado e pesquisas setoriais. Os resultados indicam que o avanço da participação feminina está relacionado à maior inserção das mulheres no universo esportivo, à influência das redes sociais e ao fortalecimento da presença das apostas no cotidiano cultural. Além disso, observa-se que as mulheres tendem a adotar comportamentos mais cautelosos em relação ao risco. Conclui-se que o mercado está em processo de amadurecimento e que a compreensão desse público é importante para estratégias mais eficientes de marketing e desenvolvimento de produtos.",2026,Silva,Revista fisio&terapia.,10.69849/ba9njd54,,https://doi.org/10.69849/ba9njd54,und,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en;crossref;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1164,O papel dos influenciadores digitais na promoção de jogos de apostas online: uma análise sobre as práticas publicitárias e a proteção do consumidor The role of digital influencers in promoting online betting games: an analysis of advertising practices and consumer protection,"Este artigo analisa a responsabilidade dos influenciadores digitais na promoção de jogos de azar online, focando nas implicações jurídicas relacionadas à publicidade enganosa e abusiva. O objetivo principal é investigar até que ponto os influenciadores podem ser responsabilizados pelas campanhas publicitárias de jogos de azar, considerando a legislação brasileira, como o Código de Defesa do Consumidor. A pesquisa foi conduzida por meio de uma revisão bibliográfica, com base em estudos sobre regulamentações nacionais e internacionais, além da análise de casos judiciais envolvendo influenciadores e plataformas de jogos de azar. O estudo também abordou conceitos como publicidade enganosa, abusiva e a responsabilidade dos influenciadores digitais nas redes sociais. Os resultados evidenciam que, apesar da legislação brasileira prever mecanismos aptos à proteção dos consumidores, existem lacunas na regulamentação que dificultam a aplicação eficiente das leis no ambiente digital. Foi identificado que muitos influenciadores promovem jogos de azar sem esclarecimentos adequados sobre os riscos financeiros, o que permite a caracterização de práticas vedadas pelo ordenamento. Conclui-se pela necessidade de aprimoramento normativo no que diz respeito à possibilidade de responsabilização dos influenciadores envolvidos em campanhas publicitárias de jogos de azar. A pesquisa aponta para a importância da criação de normas mais específicas que regulamentem essas práticas no ambiente digital, visando à proteção dos consumidores. Ademais, destaca-se a relevância de que estudos futuros aprofundem a análise dos impactos dessas campanhas sobre os indivíduos e da efetividade das regulamentações atualmente vigentes.",2026,Silva,Academia de Direito,10.24302/acaddir.v8.6419,,https://doi.org/10.24302/acaddir.v8.6419,,crossref:journal-article,crossref,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1165,Operational non-invariance: event definition and temporal resolution determine the sign of the transactional contrast in gambling payment data,"This project contains the complete reproduction package for the article ""Operational non-invariance: event definition and temporal resolution determine the sign of the transactional contrast in gambling payment data."" The central objective of this research is to investigate how the operational definition of a gambling event and the temporal resolution of observation shape the behavioral and financial conclusions drawn from transactional gambling data. The study starts from a metrological observation: research comparing player behavior using different event definitions — for example, an endogenous session-based definition (D0) versus fixed time windows (≤1h, ≤6h, ≤24h) — often produces opposite signs for the same phenomenon. Our work shows that this conflict is not a sampling artifact but a systematic property of the observation channel × estimator pair. We use three data sources: (i) public online sports betting and casino datasets from the literature (Mendeley, Transparency Project); (ii) anonymized Brazilian cooperative banking data on payments and transfers linked to gambling operators; and (iii) simulations of self-exciting point processes with negative-control calibration. The methodology combines non-parametric statistics (account-level bootstrap, risk-set matching, placebo reallocations), Hawkes intensity estimation across multiple temporal resolutions, and negative-control tests to validate conclusions. The expected and obtained results are: Proven operational non-invariance: at sub-daily resolution (exact, 15-minute, 1-hour), the endogenous D0 definition produces a positive contrast, while short fixed windows produce a negative contrast, with non-overlapping confidence intervals. This shows that the sign of ""chasing"" depends on how the event is defined. Collapse under aggregated resolution: when analysis is performed at daily or weekly resolution, intraday information is lost, fixed-window contrasts degenerate to zero, and D0 saturates at values determined by the discretization grid. This implies that aggregated-data studies cannot distinguish mechanism from measurement artifact. Failure of balance control as an isolated identifier: the available proxy for player cash flow (deposit minus withdrawal) is not identifiable in the dataset, limiting interpretations about ""loss chasing driven by liquidity."" Negative control and gate rejection: the research incorporates a pre-registration of calibration gates (G4/G5) that failed validation. The results confirm that Hawkes self-excitation can be confounded with persistent dispersion or seasonality, reinforcing that clinical interpretation of η̂ (estimated contagion intensity) requires intraday resolution and negative-control validation. The final output is a manuscript ready for submission to an international scientific journal, accompanied by a complete reproduction package (scripts, results, hashes, data provenance) allowing external auditing of all figures and tables. The project is a collaboration between SAVE Tecnologia em Saúde Mental, which develops predictive infrastructure for detecting risk-related behaviors in financial portfolios, and applied researchers in statistics, data science, and mental health. Expected impact We expect this work to: (a) establish a metrological vocabulary for behavioral gambling research using transactional data; (b) define minimum identifiability conditions for inferences about ""chasing"" and ""loss chasing""; (c) guide intraday data collection by financial institutions and credit cooperatives monitoring client risk; and (d) provide a methodological foundation for future studies with validated clinical outcomes.",2026,Silva,OSF Registries,10.17605/osf.io/gc8hj,,https://doi.org/10.17605/osf.io/gc8hj,,datacite:StudyRegistration/Pre-registration | openalex:preprint,openalex;datacite,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1166,Os impactos das apostas online de quota fixa na sociedade,"O presente artigo visa a esclarecer tópicos relevantes sobre as apostas online (bets) no âmbito do Direito Desportivo e na sociedade, tendo em vista que a disponibilização de apostas esportivas, no Brasil, vem desencadeando o endividamento das famílias, o que leva parte significativa da sociedade a um comportamento financeiro de altíssimo risco, prejudica consideravelmente a economia doméstica, o comércio varejista e o desenvolvimento social, diante do fato de que essa prática reiterada poderá evoluir para um comportamento compulsivo por parte de alguns indivíduos (transtorno do jogo patológico), o que, consequentemente, implicará o aumento no endividamento das famílias brasileiras, principalmente entre aqueles que veem neste tipo de aposta uma forma de solução rápida para suas dificuldades financeiras. Importante salientar que as bets têm como objeto principal o futebol, já que este esporte coletivo é o mais popular do mundo e, de acordo com os dados da Federação Internacional de Futebol (FIFA), cerca de 270 milhões de pessoas atuam em atividades diretamente relacionadas ao esporte. O mercado de apostas esportivas tem gerado bastante interesse dos setores ligados ao esporte profissional, sobretudo o futebol. Em 2022, dos vinte clubes da Série A do Campeonato Brasileiro de Futebol, apenas o Palmeiras não era patrocinado por alguma casa de apostas esportivas (Brito, 2022, n.p.). Desta forma, as bets uniram o útil ao agradável, ou seja, uniu a paixão que os brasileiros têm pelo futebol e a tentativa imediata de rápida solução para as suas dificuldades financeiras, o que cria, assim, um comportamento compulsivo perigoso por parte de alguns indivíduos. Estudos recentes, realizados após o advento da Lei n.º 14.790/2023 (Lei das Bets), vêm estabelecendo uma ligação forte e direta entre a prática descontrolada de apostas (facilitada pela ausência de regras mais efetivas de limitação ao jogo compulsivo) e o agravamento do nível de endividamento das famílias brasileiras (Charchat & Medeiros, 2024, n.p.).Esse assunto é um tema recente e desconhecido por grande parte dos doutores da lei; como a bibliografia a respeito é escassa, sua discussão depende de artigos, colunas, e da interpretação das próprias leis.",2026,Silva,Revista de Gestão e Negócios do Esporte,,,,pt,openalex:article | openalex_non_en:article,openalex;openalex_non_en,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1168,The Attention Factor: The Speculative Risk You May Already Own,"Cryptocurrency and equity markets have become linked-and the linkage is intensifying. Bitcoin now shares roughly a quarter of its return variation with world equities during periods of elevated speculative participation, while gold shares near zero. An asset with no shared business fundamentals-cash flows, earnings, or production linkages has developed meaningful co-movement with equity markets. For allocators, understanding this linkage is not a crypto question-it is a portfolio risk question. We therefore test whether the linkage is entirely explained by shared exposure to economy-wide conditions-global market returns and risk appetite shifts. It is not. After removing these systematic channels, a residual connectedness survives-but not uniformly. The residual is largest for firms whose revenues depend mechanically on speculative participation (DraftKings, Robinhood, Coinbase) and for sentiment-driven strategies (BUZZ Social Sentiment ETF). For institutionally priced benchmarks like the Nasdaq-100 and AI stocks, residual connectedness drops to the level explained by shared market exposure alone-despite their popularity. This pattern suggests a common cause. Our hypothesis: the linkage transmits through shared marginal investors. A speculative cohort-retail traders active across crypto exchanges, zero-day options, sports betting, and commission-free brokerages-sets prices in multiple markets simultaneously. When this cohort's sentiment shifts, it creates correlated movements across every venue they participate in. Crypto, having no fundamental equity linkage, serves as the cleanest signal of this transmission. We interpret this transmission as an Attention factor-capital-backed collective conviction expressed by a speculative cohort active across multiple markets. The key finding is not binary. Every equity investor carries some speculative sentiment exposure through the market itself-crypto co-moves with world equities broadly, meaning this channel is already embedded in market returns. What varies is how much additional connectedness specific equities carry beyond this market-level dose. Thematic growth funds, small-cap indices, and social-sentiment strategies concentrate it. The relevant question for allocators is not whether to add crypto, but how much speculative sentiment exposure already exists in the portfolio-and where on the spectrum their holdings sit.",2026,Silva,SSRN Electronic Journal,10.2139/ssrn.6277718,,https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6277718,und,openaire:Article | openalex:preprint,openalex;openaire,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1169,"The Underground World of Influencer Trading Card Gambling or ""Breaking""","This research explores the emerging phenomenon of ""breaking"", a practice whereby people, often influencers or card shop owners, open trading card packs in front of a live audience, selling randomized or selected packs to their viewers. Using a netnographic approach, I investigate three major online communities ""breakers"" use to facilitate the breaking practice. Initial participant observation and data includes 200+ social media posts, 20+ hours of video, and significant participant observation in live channels. Preliminary findings suggest that the power of influencers combined with the gambling psychology of collectible trading cards create a highly persuasive environment where community members are socially celebrated and encouraged to continue to purchase or ""gamble"" in front of a large audience. Major themes include: community-seeking, peer-pressure, belonging, and parasocial relationships. These findings suggest that trading card ""breaking"" has some parallels with the emergence of sports betting, particularly the social aspect and involvement of influencers. The findings also suggest a glorification and valorization of consumer participation in gambling, particularly when influencers are opening packs in front of large audiences.",2026,Simpson,Digital Scholarship - UNLV (University of Nevada Reno),,,,,openalex:conference-paper,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1170,Cross-Cultural Adaptations of Gambling Treatments for East Asians: A Comprehensive Scoping Review and Strategic Recommendations,,2026,Sinclair,Current Addiction Reports,10.1007/s40429-026-00780-w,,https://doi.org/10.1007/s40429-026-00780-w,en,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,cites Tran 2024,,,,
R1171,Gambling Advertising During the UEFA Euro Football Championship: A Frequency and Content Analysis in TV Coverage and Social Media,"Abstract: Aims: According to the German State Treaty on Gambling, gambling advertising must not be excessive. However, what counts as excessive is not defined, nor are there any frameworks for classifying advertising. The present study therefore quantifies and classifies gambling advertising during a specific sports event. Methodology: 11 matches of the 2024 European Football Championship were analyzed with respect to frequency and type of gambling advertising. Besides, the social media accounts of 10 sports betting providers were examined. The Meta Ad Library was used to analyze paid-for advertisements. Results: A high volume of gambling advertising is prevalent (n = 5,914), especially during TV broadcasts, where it mostly appears on pitchside hoardings without age restrictions or warnings. On social media (n = 2,645), gambling providers mainly rely on content marketing for organic advertising (1,542), whereas paid-for advertisements (1,103) are more direct and targeted towards a younger audience. Conclusions: Due to the high advertising volume and the room for improvement regarding the implementation of social responsibility measures, it remains uncertain whether the objectives of the Treaty, aimed at protecting the population from gambling-related harm, can be fully achieved. The scope, content, and strategies of these advertisements raise concerns, particularly about the risks for children and adolescents.",2026,Singer,SUCHT - Zeitschrift für Wissenschaft und Praxis / Journal of Addiction Research and Practice,10.1024/0939-5911/a000980,,https://doi.org/10.1024/0939-5911/a000980,en,openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1172,SPORTS BETTING: JUDICIAL INTERPRETATION AND LEGAL CHALLENGES IN INDIA,"This paper explores the jurisprudential evolution of gaming and sports betting laws in India, analyzing the ongoing conflict between archaic colonial statutes and the dynamic realities of the digital economy. Historically, the Indian judiciary has served as the de facto regulator of the industry, establishing the ""preponderance of skill"" test to distinguish between constitutionally protected business activities under Article 19(1)(g) and prohibited games of chance (res extra commercium). Through a comprehensive analysis of landmark judgments—ranging from R.M.D. Chamarbaugwala (1957) to Varun Gumber (2017)—the research traces how the courts have consistently defended skill-based digital and physical enterprises against disproportionate and arbitrary state-level bans. However, the paper highlights a contemporary constitutional crisis triggered by the recent enactment of the Promotion and Regulation of Online Gaming Act (PROGA), 2025. By imposing a blanket prohibition on all ""Online Money Games"" regardless of the underlying skill element, PROGA 2025 seeks to override decades of established judicial precedent. The study critically evaluates the ongoing legal challenges to the Act, specifically focusing on the Union's legislative competence, the disruption of the federal structure, and the violation of fundamental rights. Finally, it examines the counterproductive outcomes of this prohibitionist legislative approach, notably the proliferation of a $100 billion offshore shadow market and the inadvertent criminalization of legitimate professional sports. The paper concludes that the upcoming 2026 Supreme Court hearings will be a watershed moment, determining both the survival of a multi-billion-dollar industry and the boundaries of parliamentary power over State subjects in the digital age. Keywords: Sports Betting, Games of Skill vs. Chance, PROGA 2025, Judicial Interpretation, Article 19(1)(g)",2026,SINGH,Indian Journal of Legal Review,10.65393/okxm4852,,https://doi.org/10.65393/okxm4852,und,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R1173,Fantasy Sports App Participation and Its Impact on Sports Consumption Among Indian Youth,"Fantasy sports platforms have changed how young people in India consume and engage with sport, resulting in a shift from passive spectators to active participants who make choices, analyze player statistics, and compete for either monetary or social gain. This study examines the effects of fantasy sports participation on sports consumption behaviors in Indian youth aged 18-25, and how the regulatory ban on real-money fantasy contests, effective in 2025, influenced these consumption behaviors. This study follows a mixed-method explanatory sequential design, integrating quantitative survey data collected from 105 valid respondents with qualitative interviews to capture both statistical and experiential perspectives. During the quantitative phase, a within-subject pre-post design compared self-reported engagement in sport before the ban and after the ban in three areas of interest: hours of watching live matches, OTT subscriptions, and self-rated interest in sport. Analyzing for changes in the self-reported engagement metrics consisted of paired-sample t-tests and Wilcoxon signed-rank tests, with regression analysis as a way to control for demographics and motivation. Results reveal a significant decline in sports consumption post-ban: average weekly viewing hours fell by 2.3, OTT subscriptions dropped by 0.28, and sports interest decreased by 2.3 points on a 7-point scale (p &amp;lt; 0.001). Qualitative insights confirmed that the absence of monetary incentives and peer competition reduced both motivation and emotional attachment to sports. The findings suggest that fantasy sports act as a behavioral catalyst for sports engagement, amplifying consumption through informational, motivational, and social pathways. The study concludes that while the ban curbed potential gambling risks, it also weakened the broader sports consumption ecosystem. Policymakers should adopt calibrated regulation emphasizing responsible gaming and transparency rather than outright prohibition. The paper contributes empirically grounded evidence to the literature on digital fandom, gamified engagement, and regulatory policy in India's evolving sports economy.",2026,Sinha,Elsevier BV,10.2139/ssrn.6219598,,https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6219598,und,crossref:posted-content | openaire:Article | openalex:preprint,openalex;crossref;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1174,A randomized double-blind sham-controlled preliminary study of a 5-week protocol of repetitive transcranial magnetic stimulation (rTMS) combined with cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) for gambling disorder in Indonesia,"Gambling disorder (GD) has increased in prevalence particularly in Indonesia where online gambling predominates. Gambling harm may involve not only individuals with GD but also their significant others. This preliminary study aims to investigate the efficacy of repetitive transcranial magnetic stimulation (rTMS) in conjunction with cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) compared to sham rTMS with CBT in treating individuals with GD. Twenty seven participants diagnosed with GD were randomly assigned to receive either active or sham rTMS over five weeks, alongside a standardized CBT program. Outcomes were assessed at multiple time points using various standardized measures. This protocol was safe and well-tolerated, with minimal adverse events (adverse event rate: 7.2%). Both groups displayed significant reductions in gambling symptoms measured by the Gambling Symptom Assessment Scale. However, no significant differences were observed between the active and sham rTMS groups. The active rTMS group demonstrated faster reductions in gambling craving [B: 2.63 (95% CI 0.55 to 4.70), p: 0.015] and gambling-related cognition, particularly in the domains of gambling expectancies [B: 1.84 (95% CI 0.98 to 2.71), p ≤ 0.001] and the perceived inability to stop gambling [B: 1.70 (95% CI 0.36 to 3.04), p: 0.014]. The results suggest that rTMS may enhance CBT outcomes in treating GD by modulating craving and cognitive biases associated with gambling. Further research is warranted to optimize intervention parameters and assess the long-term effects of rTMS in GD treatment.",2026,Siste,Addictive Behaviors Reports,10.1016/j.abrep.2026.100722,42389422,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.abrep.2026.100722,en,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,cites Tran 2024,,,,
R1175,"Law of Nino: A Unified Probabilistic and Multi-Agent Framework for Predictive Modeling in Sports, Mathematics, and Physics","We present the Law of Nino / NMSM-model, a novel probabilistic multi-agent framework for predictive modeling validated over five Premier League seasons (2021/22–2025/26). Integrating δ-formula, Hybrid Core, PSS, Ω(t), Backward Seed, Möbius-8 symmetry, and Poisson processes, the model achieves a Brier-score of 0.0398 (98.4% reliability) and an average hit-rate of 82.2% across 1,530 matches. The framework is adaptable beyond sports, capable of addressing mathematical problems (Fibonacci sequences, prime numbers, combinatorial proofs) and physical phenomena (Monte Carlo simulations in particle physics, cosmology). Applications include sports betting optimization, scenario analysis, and scientific modeling.",2026,Smilde,Zenodo,10.5281/zenodo.18815935,,https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18815935,und,datacite:Text/ | openaire:Other literature type,datacite;openaire,2,False,True,False,,,,,
R1176,"Decisions at Play: Influence of Gambling Advertisements and Influencer Content during FIFA World Cup 2026 on Attitudes, Cognitions, and Gambling Initiation","This project investigates how exposure to gambling advertisements, including sports betting, and influencer gambling-related content during the 2026 FIFA World Cup is associated with gambling-related attitudes, cognitions, and behaviour among adults in Germany. Major sporting events are characterised by heightened visibility of gambling promotions across television and digital media, which may contribute to the normalisation of gambling, to the initiation or intensification of gambling behaviour as well as the reinforcement of gambling-related cognitive distortions. Data will be collected at three timepoints: before the tournament, during the tournament, and after the tournament. Participants will self-report their exposure to gambling-related content, gambling attitudes and expectancies, gambling-related cognitive distortions, motivation to gamble, gambling behaviour (including initiation, frequency, and spending), and gambling-related problems. The study further examines whether these associations are stronger among individuals with known vulnerability factors for gambling-related harm. The study aims to improve understanding of the associations between gambling-related media exposure during major sporting events and changes in gambling-related cognition and behaviour over time, with potential implications for responsible gambling and advertising policies.",2026,Smith,OSF Registries,10.17605/osf.io/s3jud,,https://doi.org/10.17605/osf.io/s3jud,,datacite:StudyRegistration/Pre-registration | openalex:preprint,openalex;datacite,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1177,"Math, Data, and Cognitive Bias: Educating Teens to Make Informed Decisions About Gambling","This presentation introduces the Gambling Awareness Initiative (GAI), a program designed to educate teens about the risks of sports gambling using data, probability, and cognitive-bias research. While many interventions focus on stories of addiction, GAI emphasizes the math behind gambling and the ways cognitive biases—such as the illusion of control—affect decision-making. Participants will see how simple simulations, coin-flip activities, and expected-value visualizations reveal the true odds and long-term outcomes of gambling. The session demonstrates how applied statistical reasoning can empower teens to recognize and resist harmful gambling behaviors. Implications extend to educators, parents, and community advocates seeking evidence-based approaches to prevention, bridging research and practice in a highly engaging, interactive format.",2026,Smith,Digital Scholarship - UNLV (University of Nevada Reno),,,,,openalex:conference-paper,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1178,Beyond the Bet: An Updated Scoping Review on Sports Gambling,"ABSTRACT Background: Technological advances and changes in legislation have driven the proliferation of sports betting in recent years. Therefore, understanding who is at risk of sports betting-related consequences and how to mitigate harm is essential. Objectives: The present scoping review aimed to provide an updated examination of the correlates of sports betting and interventions for sports betting. Methods: Articles published between April 2022 and June 2025 were screened, and 60 studies were eligible for inclusion. Results: Most studies explicitly examined or included correlates of sports betting, and a small minority focused on interventions for sports betting. Across studies, sports bettors were most often younger men with higher income and education levels. Psychological factors such as impulsivity, sensation seeking, competitiveness, and cognitive distortions (eg, illusion of control) were consistently associated with more frequent and problematic betting. Social influences, including peer norms, sports fandom, and exposure to advertising, were also linked to engagement and harm. Evidence on interventions remains limited but suggests modest benefits of responsible gambling tools, including precommitment, and safer gambling messages. Conclusions: Overall, findings underscore the need for more targeted approaches to prevent and minimize potential harms associated with sports betting. Contexte: Les progrès technologiques et les changements dans la législation ont favorisé la prolifération des paris sportifs ces dernières années. Il est donc essentiel de comprendre qui est exposé aux conséquences liées aux paris sportifs et comment en atténuer les effets néfastes. Objectifs: La présente revue exploratoire visait à fournir une analyse actualisée des facteurs associés aux paris sportifs et des interventions en la matière. Méthodes: Les articles publiés entre avril 2022 et juin 2025 ont été examinés, et 60 études ont été jugées éligibles pour inclusion. Résultats: La plupart des études examinaient explicitement ou incluaient les corrélats des paris sportifs, et une petite minorité se concentrait sur les interventions en matière de paris sportifs. Dans l’ensemble des études, les parieurs sportifs étaient le plus souvent des hommes jeunes disposant de revenus et d’un niveau d'éducation plus élevés. Des facteurs psychologiques tels que l’impulsivité, la recherche de sensations fortes, la compétitivité et les distorsions cognitives (par exemple, l’illusion de contrôle) étaient systématiquement associés à des paris plus fréquents et problématiques. Les influences sociales, notamment les normes des pairs, le fanatisme sportif et l’exposition à la publicité, étaient également liées à la pratique et aux effets néfastes. Les données sur les interventions restent limitées, mais suggèrent des bénéfices modestes sur les outils de jeu responsable, notamment l’engagement préalable et les messages en faveur d’un jeu plus sûr. Conclusions: Dans l’ensemble, les résultats soulignent la nécessité d’adopter des approches plus ciblées pour prévenir et minimiser les effets néfastes potentiels associés aux paris sportifs.",2026,Snaychuk,The Canadian Journal of Addiction,10.1097/cxa.0000000000000278,,https://doi.org/10.1097/cxa.0000000000000278,en,crossref:journal-article | openalex:article | openalex_non_en:article | s2:JournalArticle;Review,openalex;openalex_non_en;s2;crossref,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R1179,Preventive Interventions for Safer Online Betting: A Systematic Review,A systematic review and synthesis of scientific literature on preventive interventions for safer online gambling and their effectiveness.,2026,Soborun,OSF Preprints (OSF Preprints),10.17605/osf.io/s94a2,,https://doi.org/10.17605/osf.io/s94a2,,datacite:StudyRegistration/Pre-registration | openalex:preprint,openalex;datacite,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1180,PATTERNS AND PREVALENCE OF SPORTS BETTING AMONGST UNDERGRADUATE SPORTS ENTHUSIAST,"Sports betting has transformed from an ancient pastime into a multi-billion-dollar global industry, influencing economies, sports culture, and individual behaviours. This article critically examines the evolution of sports betting, its global and national trends, and its growing prevalence among Nigerian youth, particularly among university students and sports enthusiasts. While the industry generates substantial revenue, supports employment, and enhances sports engagement, it also raises concerns about addiction, financial distress, and regulatory loopholes. The accessibility of online betting platforms, coupled with aggressive marketing and celebrity endorsements, has fuelled increased participation, often at the expense of financial stability and academic performance. Additionally, this paper explores the socioeconomic impact of betting, highlighting how economic hardship and peer influence contribute to widespread gambling behaviours. With Nigeria emerging as a major betting hub in Africa, a strategic balance between economic benefits and social responsibility is crucial. Strengthening regulatory frameworks, promoting financial literacy, and implementing responsible gambling measures are imperative to mitigate associated risks. This article advocates for a holistic approach that safeguards vulnerable populations while ensuring the sustainability of the industry within ethical boundaries.",2026,Soladoye-Adewole,Journal of the Nigeria Association of Sports Science and Medicine,10.66986/jnassm.2026.1901.33-j,,https://doi.org/10.66986/jnassm.2026.1901.33-j,und,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R1181,Schema on the Inside: A Two-Phase Fine-Tuning Method for High-Efficiency Text-to-SQL at Scale,"Applying large, proprietary API-based language models to text-to-SQL tasks poses a significant industry challenge: reliance on massive, schema-heavy prompts results in prohibitive per-token API costs and high latency, hindering scalable production deployment. We present a specialized, self-hosted 8B-parameter model designed for a conversational bot in CriQ, a sister app to Dream11, India's largest fantasy sports platform with over 250 million users, that answers user queries about cricket statistics. Our novel two-phase supervised fine-tuning approach enables the model to internalize the entire database schema, eliminating the need for long-context prompts. This reduces input tokens by over 99%, from a 17k-token baseline to fewer than 100, and replaces costly external API calls with efficient local inference. The resulting system achieves 98.4% execution success and 92.5% semantic accuracy, substantially outperforming a prompt-engineered baseline using Google's Gemini Flash 2.0 (95.6% execution, 89.4% semantic accuracy). These results demonstrate a practical path toward high-precision, low-latency text-to-SQL applications using domain-specialized, self-hosted language models in large-scale production environments.",2026,Soni,Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence,10.1609/aaai.v40i47.41446,,https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v40i47.41446,en,datacite:Audiovisual/Conference talk | datacite:Preprint/Article | openaire:Article; Conference object; Preprint | openalex:conference-paper | openalex:other | s2:JournalArticle;Conference,openalex;s2;datacite;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R1182,Apostas on-line e saúde mental em adultos: Revisão crítica da literatura com metanálise exploratória de ansiedade e estresse,"A expansão das plataformas de apostas exige distinguir participação recreativa, gravidade do jogo e sofrimento psicológico. Este artigo analisa a relação entre apostas on-line e saúde mental, com atenção às apostas esportivas, à depressão e ao risco suicida. Realizou-se revisão crítica com busca dirigida no PubMed, na BVS e no Portal de Periódicos CAPES, complementada por textos de periódicos e repositórios. A discussão reuniu 18 estudos primários e sete sínteses científicas. A síntese quantitativa exploratória reuniu dois estudos transversais em adultos, com 6.283 participantes, que informaram correlações de Spearman entre gravidade do jogo on-line e ansiedade ou estresse. Utilizaram-se transformação de Fisher, efeitos aleatórios de DerSimonian–Laird e intervalos conservadores de Hartung–Knapp modificados. As estimativas combinadas foram 0,117 para ansiedade e 0,091 para estresse; os intervalos conservadores incluíram ausência de associação. A heterogeneidade da ansiedade foi elevada, enquanto o resultado de estresse foi dominado pelo estudo maior. Depressão, ideação suicida e comparações entre modalidades foram examinadas narrativamente, por incompatibilidade das medidas. A síntese narrativa sustenta uma crítica à promoção irrestrita das apostas, com efeitos experimentais de incentivos sobre decisões e evidência de danos financeiros. A metanálise não estabelece causalidade ou risco específico de plataformas. Conclui-se pela necessidade de estudos longitudinais brasileiros, medidas por produto e avaliações clínicas que considerem perdas financeiras, controle do comportamento e comorbidades.",2026,Sousa,Journal of Social Issues and Health Sciences (JSIHS),10.5281/zenodo.23113261,,https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23113261,pt,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1183,"APOSTAS ESPORTIVAS E A REGULAMENTAÇÃO À LUZ DO CÓDIGO DE DEFESA DO CONSUMIDOR: DESAFIOS, PERSPECTIVAS E IMPACTOS SOCIAIS NO ORDENAMENTO JURÍDICO BRASILEIRO","Introdução Nas últimas décadas, o avanço tecnológico transformou as relações de consumo, especialmente com a expansão dos serviços digitais. Nesse cenário, cresceram atividades online que envolvem riscos aos usuários, exigindo maior atenção do ordenamento jurídico. A facilidade de acesso às plataformas virtuais e a intensa divulgação nas redes sociais ampliaram o alcance dessas práticas, atingindo um público cada vez mais diverso e vulnerável. Esse contexto demonstra a necessidade de mecanismos eficazes de proteção jurídica, diante da assimetria de informações entre fornecedores e usuários. A publicidade digital, muitas vezes atrativa e persuasiva, pode induzir o consumidor a decisões precipitadas, sem plena compreensão dos riscos. Além disso, a atuação de influenciadores digitais reforça esse cenário, já que seu poder de convencimento impacta diretamente os seguidores, nem sempre observando os deveres de transparência e boa-fé. Diante disso, é essencial analisar como os princípios da responsabilidade civil e da proteção do consumidor podem ser aplicados para garantir equilíbrio nessas relações. A falta de fiscalização efetiva e a dificuldade de responsabilização dos agentes envolvidos contribuem para a insegurança jurídica e para prejuízos financeiros e sociais. Assim, o presente estudo busca examinar a efetividade dos instrumentos jurídicos disponíveis para assegurar a proteção dos consumidores no ambiente digital, diante dos desafios das novas formas de consumo e da crescente influência midiática.Objetivo: Analisar, sob uma perspectiva jurídica e social, a aplicação do Código de Defesa do Consumidor (Lei nº 8.078/1990) nas atividades de apostas esportivas e jogos online, que foram regulamentadas pela Lei nº 14.790/2023, buscando entender como o ordenamento jurídico brasileiro pode assegurar proteção efetiva e ágil aos consumidores diante de práticas abusivas e da influência exercida por plataformas e influenciadores digitais.",2026,Souza,"Revista Ibero-Americana de Humanidades, Ciências e Educação",10.51891/rease.v12i5.26862,,https://doi.org/10.51891/rease.v12i5.26862,und,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en;crossref;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1184,Critical financial education: a mathematical study on investmentsand games of chance as an instrument for awareness and citizenship inbasic education,"Based on the incorporation of Financial Education as a curricular component within the basic education curriculum in the state of Paraná, as well as the significant growth of online betting and electronic gaming platforms in Brazil, this study aims to address the mathematical and probabilistic aspects of financial investments, presenting basic concepts related to real financial applications alongside those termed here as illusory investments, which have contributed to the rising indebtedness of a significant portion of the Brazilian population, compromising household income and elevating the risks associated with gambling addiction. As an educational product, we present a didactic proposal involving an online platform that encompasses three illusory investments and mathematically demonstrates their disadvantages. Through this approach, we hope to contribute to the development of critical and logical-mathematical thinking among Basic Education students regarding games of chance and electronic betting, thereby fostering greater awareness regarding promotional materials for illusory investments.",2026,Souza,Institutional Repository of the Federal Technological University of Paraná (RIUT) (Federal University of Technology – Paraná),,,,pt,openalex:dissertation,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1185,"Direito, tecnologia da informação e acesso à justiça no contexto esportivo","À medida que as apostas esportivas de quota fixas entram no Brasil, o assunto continua interessante; no entanto, a regulamentação das apostas esportivas foi além de uma questão econômica e fiscal restrita, transformando-se em uma conversa mais ampla sobre questões de autenticidade esportiva, conformidade e combate à lavagem de dinheiro (AML). Este artigo destaca os desafios de responsabilidade regulatória e legal que acompanham a digitalização, agravados pelas vulnerabilidades dos atores esportivos. Este estudo fornece, subsequentemente, uma visão sobre a interação entre Direito, Tecnologia da Informação e Acesso à Justiça no ambiente esportivo. Argumenta que a implementação da integridade e a contenção da atividade criminosa, apoiadas por tecnologias de monitoramento, constituem os mecanismos decisivos que garantem a segurança jurídica e o acesso à justiça esportiva. Identifica a legislação a ser seguida, estratégias de conformidade e vulnerabilidades do sistema, como deficiências de governança e a possibilidade de o pessoal esportivo ser atraído para manipulação de resultados, e propõe a elaboração de uma política regulatória que alcance um equilíbrio entre contabilizar o ganho financeiro de tal atividade e preservar a moralidade e lealdade esportiva.",2026,Souza,Revista Fronteiras Interdisciplinares do Direito,10.23925/2596-3333.v1n1.76272,,https://doi.org/10.23925/2596-3333.v1n1.76272,,crossref:journal-article | openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en;crossref,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1187,"Arbitrage Bounds and Kelly-Optimal Hedging in Fixed-Odds Sports Betting Markets: A Fee-Adjusted, Time-Indexed Approach","We develop a formal framework for arbitrage and hedging in twooutcome, fixed-odds sports betting markets, motivated by a practical hedging problem arising in soccer wagering. We derive a fee-adjusted, time-indexed arbitrage condition showing that a guaranteed-profit position is structurally unavailable within a single bookmaker's simultaneous quote, due to the bookmaker's built-in margin, but occasionally attainable across two points in time as quoted odds drift. We then extend the single-bet Kelly criterion to the two-outcome hedged case under a symmetric proportional fee, deriving a closed-form optimal hedge fraction that reduces to the standard Kelly formula in the absence of a prior position. This framework resolves an apparent tension between expectedprofit maximisation and risk minimisation by showing both to be special cases of a single expected-log-growth-maximising calculation. A preliminary check against five seasons of English Premier League data illustrates the arbitrage condition in practice, finding that it is satisfied in a modest but non-trivial fraction of matches, and we discuss the distinction between the existence of such windows and their practical exploitability as a direction for future empirical work. &lt;div&gt; &lt;br&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div&gt; &lt;br&gt; &lt;/div&gt;",2026,Srivastav,Elsevier BV,10.2139/ssrn.7114860,,https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7114860,und,crossref:posted-content | openaire:Article | openalex:preprint,openalex;crossref;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1188,Gambling behavior and problem risk by coaching status in individuals with athletic backgrounds from an epidemiological sample,"The popularity and expansion of sports wagering has highlighted the betting behavior of athletes, particularly at college and professional levels. Far less attention, however, has been paid to the gambling behavior of coaches, despite their immersion in sports environments saturated with gambling opportunities and their potential influence on athletes’ attitudes and behaviors. The present study utilized a subsample of individuals with athletic backgrounds from an epidemiological study (N = 1,778), including current coaches (n = 161), former coaches (n = 595), and individuals who never coached (n = 1,022). Bivariate comparisons by coaching status found that current coaches gambled at the highest frequency, in more venues, across more activities, including sports and fantasy sports betting, and reported the highest rates of problem gambling. In a multivariate linear regression, current coach status was associated with a 2.33-point higher Problem Gambling Severity Index score (p < .001) compared to non-coaches; former coaches did not significantly differ from non-coaches. Among current coaches, problem gambling was associated with being an NCAA athlete, current sports participation, perceiving family and friend participation in sports betting, depression, drug and alcohol problems, risky sex, and excessive video/internet gaming. These findings suggest coaches require their own education and intervention, and should be included in prevention programs targeting athletes.",2026,Stanmyre,International Gambling Studies,10.1080/14459795.2026.2697456,,https://doi.org/10.1080/14459795.2026.2697456,en,openalex:article,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1189,"Gambling in fraternity and sorority life: leadership perspectives on social influences, risk, and prevention.","Objective: To examine Greek life leaders' perceptions of gambling prevalence, peer influences, capacity for member support, and prevention strategies. Participants: Eleven Greek life leaders from a northeastern university were recruited in Summer/Fall 2025. Methods: The qualitative study used semi-structured interviews analyzed using a thematic approach combining collaborative deductive and inductive coding. Results: Gambling-notably online sports betting and poker-was described as widespread in fraternities, where it is normalized within the social culture and integrated into recruitment and other social activities. Leaders noted that the private nature of online gambling makes problematic involvement difficult to identify. Participants highlighted limited gambling-specific resources and a lack of university-level gambling policy and education. Conclusions: Findings illustrate how fraternity social environments may normalize and reinforce gambling while its increasingly online nature makes escalating problems difficult to detect. These insights highlight the need for institutional gambling policies and prevention initiatives tailored to Greek life, ideally incorporating personal testimony.",2026,Stanmyre,Journal of American college health : J of ACH,10.1080/07448481.2026.2746416,42875419,https://doi.org/10.1080/07448481.2026.2746416,eng,openalex:article | pubmed:Journal Article | s2:JournalArticle,pubmed;openalex;s2,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1190,Guiding Gambling Policy and Problem Gambling Treatment Decisions Using ArcGIS StoryMaps,"The expansion of online wagering has highlighted problem gambling as a growing public health concern. Developing evidence-based methods to identify specific subgroups of individuals disproportionately impacted by gambling is critical to guide public policy and treatment service initiatives. The goal of the current study is to use GIS mapping to identify geographic areas with residents most at risk for gambling problems in a northeastern state. We created a progressive five-map ArcGIS StoryMap, culminating in a comparative risk assessment. Specifically, maps display demographic and socioeconomic indicators associated with problem gambling risk (Map 1); the proportion of residents who engaged in online sports wagering (Map 2) and online casino gambling (i.e., iGaming)(Map 3); overall online gambling prevalence and the location of land-based gambling venues, with a 20-minute drive-time analysis (Map 4); and ZIP code-level risk scores, presented in relation to in-person supports and treatment services (Map 5). Demographic and socioeconomic data were sourced from the 2022 American Community Survey, and bettor-level gambling data were extracted from yearly reports to regulators in the state. Locations of counseling and support services were identified through national and state databases and independently verified. Risk scores were calculated as weighted composites based on the prevalence and strength of indicators related to gambling problems (i.e., point-biserial correlations).",2026,Stanmyre,Digital Scholarship - UNLV (University of Nevada Reno),,,,,openalex:conference-paper,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1191,"Not just for sport: a systematic review and meta-analysis of gambling, at-risk gambling, and risk factors among athletes","Gambling opportunities, particularly for sports betting, are rapidly expanding, raising concerns about associated risks for a range of subpopulations, including athletes. This systematic review and meta-analysis examined gambling behaviours among youth, collegiate, amateur, and elite/professional athletes, assessing both participation rates and risk factors for problem gambling. Following PRISMA 2020 guidelines, five major databases and forward and backward citation searches identified 56 quantitative, English-language studies for narrative synthesis. Almost two-thirds of studies were conducted in the United States, and more than half were of college athletes. Overall, 22 studies provided sufficient data for meta-analyses on at-risk gambling. Findings indicate that athletes are generally more likely than non-athletes to engage in gambling and to do so at problematic levels, with a pooled at-risk gambling prevalence of 12.2%. Male gender and alcohol use were consistently correlated with increased gambling behaviour, while social and familial influences also were associated with problem risk, though overall examination of problem predictors was limited. Additionally, methodological weaknesses including non-probability sampling and potential response bias were common. These limitations underscore the need for more rigorous, theory-driven research to clarify how and why athletic involvement may influence gambling behaviours and related harms in the current climate.",2026,Stanmyre,International Journal of Sport and Exercise Psychology,10.1080/1612197x.2026.2722368,,https://doi.org/10.1080/1612197x.2026.2722368,en,openalex:review,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1192,Online Sports Betting Legalization and the Reallocation of Retail Investor Information Search Toward Lottery-type Stocks,"I examine whether the legalization of online sports betting is associated with a reallocation of retail investors' information search across stocks around firm earnings announcements (EAs). Prior work links legalization to a reallocation of household capital, but its association with information search has not been examined. Exploiting the staggered timing of legalization following Murphy v. NCAA, I use four treated and four matched control states over 2017-2024 and measure search using state-level Google Trends data for firm tickers. Treated and control states are already on different trajectories before any legalization, which confounds the average-level comparison. The association I can document is therefore only cross-sectional. Legalization is associated with a higher search for large, lottery-type stocks, concentrated in states and periods when sportsbook search is elevated rather than when general sports-media engagement is. The shift I can document is in the composition of retail information search rather than its level.",2026,Stark,Journal of the Arkansas Academy of Science,,,,,openalex:article,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1193,RESTRICTING SPORTSBOOK and GAMBLING ADVERTISING WITHIN FIRST AMENDMENT COMMERCIAL FREE SPEECH PROTECTIONS,"This article examines how the proliferation of legalized sports gambling and ubiquitous sportsbook advertising, now a fixture of broadcasts and live events, warrants targeted First Amendment restrictions on commercial speech to protect public health and safety. Recent studies show that these ads harm average sports fans by heightening problem gambling, while normalizing addictive behaviors among impressionable young viewers. Under the Central Hudson framework (1980), lawmakers can impose narrowly tailored limits such as time/place/manner bans on in-game ads, mandatory addiction-risk disclosures, and age-targeted safeguards that advance substantial government interests without unconstitutionally restricting speech, mirroring successful precedents for tobacco and alcohol advertising.",2026,Steed,Gaming Law Review,10.1177/25725300261469372,,https://doi.org/10.1177/25725300261469372,en,openaire:Article | openalex:editorial | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1194,From Picks to Posts: How Social Media Normalizes Sports Betting for College Athletes,"This study examined how prominent sports-betting accounts frame betting on social media and how college athletes encounter, interpret, and respond to such content. Using a mixed-methods design, this study combined a large-scale social media content analysis ( n = 38,925 posts from X) with semi-structured interviews ( n = 17) with current National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA) athletes. Findings indicated that betting-related content is highly concentrated among a small group of high-volume accounts and is frequently framed around opportunity, strategy, and entertainment, with comparatively little emphasis on gambling-related risk. Interview data revealed that college athletes experience pervasive, often unavoidable exposure to sports-betting content that contributes to perceptions of betting as a normalized component of sports culture despite institutional prohibitions. Integrating framing theory with normalization scholarship, the study proposes a feedback loop in which content production, engagement, algorithmic amplification, and repeated exposure reinforce the visibility and cultural legitimacy of sports betting. The findings have implications for college athletes’ well-being, media literacy, and responsible communication practices among media companies and sportsbook operators.",2026,Stokowski,Communication & Sport,10.1177/21674795261477691,,https://doi.org/10.1177/21674795261477691,en,crossref:journal-article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;crossref,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R1195,An Exploratory Investigation of College Student Betting Behaviors: How Pervasive is Sports Betting in the Age of Legalized Gambling?,,2026,Stone,DigitalCommons - Kennesaw State University (Kennesaw State University),,,,,openalex:article,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1196,TRANSTORNO DO JOGO: A emergência do fenômeno e as contribuições da terapia cognitivo-comportamental,"O Transtorno do Jogo é uma problemática global, que provoca prejuízos significativos nos âmbitos psicológicos, comportamentais, financeiros, familiares, ocupacionais, sociais e/ou educacionais. Esta revisão da literatura objetivou mapear o levantamento de dados referente ao Transtorno de Jogo à luz da Terapia Cognitivo-Comportamental, focando nas contribuições desta linha teórica para a compreensão e tratamento deste fenômeno emergente. Além disso, o estudo visou explorar a etiologia, os prejuízos, a prevalência, a incidência, o prognóstico e fatores de risco, e a neurobiologia do transtorno. Por meio de revisões sistemáticas, meta-análises recentes, e consulta em bibliografias clássicas, os resultados evidenciaram fortes evidências da Terapia Cognitivo-Comportamental na redução de danos associados ao transtorno do jogo, utilizando técnicas como identificação de distorções cognitivas, psicoeducação e modificação de comportamentos, por exemplo. Neste sentido, pode-se perceber que a crescente popularização dos jogos de azar demanda maior conscientização pública e investimento em pesquisas, primordialmente no que diz respeito ao pós-tratamento psicoterapêutico, para fomentar estratégias de prevenção e tratamentos acessíveis.",2026,Stuani,Psicologia e Saúde em Debate,10.22289/2446-922x.v12a1a39,,https://doi.org/10.22289/2446-922x.v12a1a39,pt,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,cites Tran 2024,,,,
R1197,"Personality Traits, Self Esteem and Perceived Controllability as Predictors of Psychological Health among Gamblers in Ado Ekiti, Ekiti State","Sports betting and other forms of gambling have increased rapidly across many African cities, including those in Nigeria, largely driven by the growth of commercial betting outlets and mobile betting platforms. Although research from high-income countries links gambling with adverse psychological outcomes, empirical evidence on the psychological determinants of gamblers’ well-being in low- and middle-income countries (LMICs) remains limited. Understanding how personality characteristics and perceived control relate to psychological health among gamblers in African settings is therefore important for informing prevention and intervention strategies. A cross-sectional survey design was employed among 300 active gamblers recruited through purposive sampling from major sports betting centres in Ado Ekiti, Nigeria. Participants completed standardized measures assessing Big Five personality traits, self-esteem, perceived controllability, and psychological health. Data were analysed using Pearson correlation, multiple regression analysis, and independent-samples t tests. Perceived controllability showed a significant positive association with psychological health (r = .12, p .05. However, extraversion (β = −.15, t = −1.69, p .05. Personality factors and perceived controllability appear to have modest but meaningful associations with gamblers’ psychological health. Interventions targeting gamblers in Nigeria may benefit from incorporating personality-informed counselling and cognitive-behavioural approaches aimed at strengthening perceived control.",2026,Sulaiman,Nigerian Journal of Social Psychology,,,,en,openalex:article,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1198,A Brief Virtual Reality Intervention Reduces Gambling Symptoms and Gambling Engagement: A Pilot Study,,2026,Sullivan,Journal of Gambling Studies,10.1007/s10899-026-10538-8,42518104,https://doi.org/10.1007/s10899-026-10538-8,en,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,cites Tran 2024,,,,
R1199,"Online Betting Apps in India: An Epidemic of Addiction, Celebrity Complicity, and Regulatory Failure",,2026,Syed,Unpublished,10.13140/rg.2.2.29629.22248,,https://doi.org/10.13140/rg.2.2.29629.22248,en,datacite:Text/Other | openalex:article,openalex;datacite,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1200,The impact of cash out availability on online betting behavior,"The rise of online sports betting, facilitated by technological innovations such as the cash-out feature, has transformed the gambling landscape. While cash-outs (a facility provided by betting operators which allows gamblers to close a bet early before the final outcome of a sports event is known) have been suggested to intensify problematic gambling behaviors, empirical studies to date have been correlational, leaving a gap in determining causal evidence. The present Registered Report investigated the direct impact of the perceived availability of the cash-out feature on various facets of gambling behavior in an online experiment. Hungarian residents with an online gambling history (N=595) were informed that they would have the chance to gamble with real money on sports events. Following random allocation, half of the participants were told that they would have the option to cash out their bets before the outcome of the sports event is known, while the other half did not have this option. Overall, the findings provided evidence that cash-out availability did not influence bet placement, wager size, or bet risk among our sample. However, the low variance in the outcomes may have limited the ability to detect subtle differences. Consequently, the null results should not be taken as conclusive evidence of no behavioral effect.",2026,Szaszi,PsyArXiv,10.31234/osf.io/rkb7a_v1,,https://doi.org/10.31234/osf.io/rkb7a_v1,und,crossref:posted-content | datacite:StudyRegistration/Pre-registration | europepmc:Preprint|src=PPR | openaire:Article | openalex:other | openalex:preprint,europepmc;openalex;crossref;datacite;openaire,5,False,False,False,,R2094,,,
R1201,Evidence-based prevention of gambling dual disorder through clinical neuroscience and precision psychiatry,"OBJECTIVE: Gambling is a common activity that becomes problematic in some vulnerable individuals, with gambling disorder (GD) now recognised as a bona fide mental/brain disorder. Several factors are associated with vulnerability to developing GD, including other mental disorders and pathological personality traits like high impulsivity. This clinical condition, referred to as Dual Gambling Disorder (GDD), better captures the broader psychopathological spectrum of GD. METHODS: This narrative review addresses recent advances in neuroscience and psychiatry that can help design more effective prevention strategies for GD. After establishing the current state of the art regarding GD/GDD from a biopsychosocial perspective, we assess the scientific evidence supporting approaches to GDD prevention. RESULTS: Following an overview of GD/GDD, we examine how precision psychiatry can not only shape therapeutic interventions but also, evidence-based prevention strategies for GD, and how these strategies align with advances in clinical neuroscience and precision psychiatry. Prevention is analyzed across multiple levels: primordial, primary, secondary, and tertiary. Finally, we outline key elements to be considered when designing scientifically grounded prevention strategies for specific target populations. CONCLUSIONS: The development of preventive strategies for GD, particularly when arising alongside other mental disorders, must be grounded in scientific evidence from neuroscience and precision psychiatry.",2026,Szerman,International Journal of Psychiatry in Clinical Practice,10.1080/13651501.2026.2621881,41609212,https://doi.org/10.1080/13651501.2026.2621881,en,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,cites Tran 2024,,,,
R1202,Penegakan Hukum Terhadap Tindak Pidana Judi Bola Online Oleh Polres Boyolali Ditinjau Dari Perspektif Undang-undang Informasi Dan Transaksi Elektronik,"The rapid development of information technology has given rise to the phenomenon of online soccer gambling, which has become the most prevalent form of cybercrime in Indonesia, with a turnover of Rp286.84 trillion projected for 2025. This study aims to analyze the characteristics of online soccer gambling and its regulation under the Law on Information and Electronic Transactions (ITE Law), as well as to examine the legal enforcement framework implemented by the Boyolali Police Department. The theories employed include Soerjono Soekanto’s theory of law enforcement, the Catur Wangsa concept, and the integrated criminal justice system. The study employs an empirical legal method with a descriptive-analytical research design. Data collection was conducted through direct interviews with investigators from the Criminal Investigation Unit of the Boyolali Police Department, as well as a literature review of relevant laws and regulations. The results indicate that online soccer gambling possesses distinct characteristics, including a borderless nature, the anonymity of perpetrators, unrestricted access at any time, and the complexity of digital transactions. Following the implementation of the National Criminal Code on January 2, 2026, investigators shifted from Article 27(2) in conjunction with Article 45(3) of the ITE Law to Articles 426 and 427 of Law No. 1 of 2023. The study concluded that existing regulations are not yet fully optimal due to extraterritorial jurisdictional loopholes and the absence of the term “online” in the Criminal Procedure Code (KUHAP), thus necessitating the establishment of a special Police Regulation for the handling of online gambling).",2026,Tamtomo,UMS Library Center of Academic Activities (Universitas Surakarta),,,,en,openalex:dissertation,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1203,Mindfulness-based interventions for gambling disorder: A systematic review,"Background and Aims: Gambling disorder (GD) presents significant psychological, financial, and social consequences. Mindfulness-based interventions (MBIs) have emerged as promising adjunctive treatments. However, the evidence base remains heterogeneous. The present systematic review evaluated the current empirical literature on MBIs for GD, focusing on their efficacy, methodological quality, and limitations. Methods: Scopus, PubMed, Web of Science, EBSCO, and PsycINFO were searched for English-language studies published between 2012 and April 2025. The final sample comprised 12 studies: five randomized controlled trials, one controlled pilot study, two repeated-measures studies, one mixed-methods study, and three single-group pretest-posttest studies. A narrative synthesis evaluated MBI impacts. Results: MBIs consistently reduced gambling frequency and cravings while enhancing psychological outcomes. Studies combining mindfulness with cognitive behavioral therapy showed significant declines in problem gambling behavior. Psychological distress and cravings also decreased notably across interventions. The mindfulness components employed varied in focus and application, adding nuance to outcome interpretation. However, it remains unclear to what extent the observed effects can be attributed to mindfulness-specific mechanisms. Discussion and Conclusions: MBIs show promise as a complementary treatment for gambling disorders, although small sample sizes and methodological limitations suggest a need for more robust research.",2026,Tannous,Journal of Behavioral Addictions,10.1556/2006.2025.00100,41632115,https://doi.org/10.1556/2006.2025.00100,en,citations:review,citations,1,True,False,False,cites Tran 2024,,,,
R1204,The Federal Gap in Sports Betting,"The modern sports betting market has outgrown the legal framework that governs it. Drawing on examples from the NBA, this article highlights four areas in which federal legislation is needed: player specific proposition bets, the rise of bettor harassment directed at players and coaches, the absence of a centralized public reporting and oversight structure, and the growing use of prediction market or event contract labeling to evade ordinary gambling regulation. This article contends that Congress should adopt a federal floor for sports betting that restricts the bet types most susceptible to manipulation, requires uniform reporting and oversight, imposes anti-harassment obligations on sportsbooks, and closes loopholes that allow sports betting to be marketed under alternative labels.",2026,Taqi,bepress Legal Repository,,,,,openalex:article,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1205,Prediction Markets as a Money Laundering Vector: The Coordinated Loss Problem,"Prediction markets have grown from a niche academic curiosity into mainstream financial infrastructure. Polymarket processed $12 billion in monthly volume in January 2026 and is now valued at $9 billion. This growth presents novel questions for compliance infrastructure that existing regulatory frameworks were not designed to anticipate. This paper identifies and analyzes a specific structural vulnerability: coordinated loss exploitation, a scheme in which illicit funds are distributed across hundreds of accounts betting on the losing side of a binary prediction contract, while a single account holds a large position on the winning side. The paper does not claim this scheme has been observed in practice. It claims the market structure makes it feasible, the regulatory environment makes it difficult to detect under current frameworks, and the cost structure makes it analytically distinctive relative to documented alternatives at approximately 2% of capital moved under stated assumptions. Version 2 incorporates a formal threat model, explicit feasibility conditions, a limitations section, simulation methodology with stated parameters, and an extension to sports betting tipping markets as a second structural environment where the same mechanism applies with additional consumer fraud implications.",2026,Tavva,SSRN Electronic Journal,10.2139/ssrn.6670038,,https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6670038,und,openaire:Article | openalex:preprint,openalex;openaire,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R1206,A Review of Gambling Addiction and Attachment Styles in the Context of Emotion Regulation Processes,"Addiction is a condition characterized by a loss of control over a substance or behavior. Gambling addiction is a type of behavioral addiction that negatively affects an individual's social functioning, and in recent years, with increasing digitalization, it has become a significant public health problem. The aim of this study is to examine the relationship between gambling addiction and attachment styles in the context of emotion regulation processes. In this study, Turkish and English studies published in the Web of Science, Scopus, PubMed, and Google Scholar databases between 2000 and 2025 were reviewed. Quantitative, qualitative, and mixed-methods peer-reviewed articles were examined, and the data were analyzed thematically. The study shows that insecure attachment styles increase the risk of gambling addiction, while secure attachment plays a protective role. Difficulties in emotion regulation stand out as an important variable mediating this relationship. In addition, escaping from negative emotions, stress, and anxiety is among the main motivations triggering gambling behavior. These findings show that gambling addiction is not only behavioral but also a multidimensional structure related to early attachment experiences and emotional regulation processes. Insecure attachment increases susceptibility to addictive behaviors through dysfunctional coping strategies. Gambling addiction is closely related to attachment styles and emotion regulation skills and should be addressed within a multidimensional and holistic psychosocial framework. In preventative measures, attachment-based approaches and interventions that improve emotion regulation skills are considered effective. In clinical practice, the use of attachment-focused interventions alongside cognitive behavioral therapy is recommended.",2026,Taze,Addiction Science Reviews,10.35365/asr.26.1.05,,https://doi.org/10.35365/asr.26.1.05,,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,cites Tran 2024,,,,
