R1485,A Psychiatric Analysis of Online Betting (Bets) (and how it relates to the dictatorship installed in Brazil),"This article presents a psychiatric analysis of the rapid growth of online betting (bets) in Brazil and its connections to the political structure of the country. Current data indicate that approximately 30% of Brazilians, mainly young men, have engaged in online betting, with alarming consequences for public health, such as unpayable debts and a fifteen-fold increase in suicide risk among gamblers. The expansion of these activities coincides with the government’s selective interest in regulating digital platforms, where strict controls on social media are justified under the pretext of protecting public welfare, while online betting remains virtually untouched. The text argues that this discrepancy reflects the interests of the so-called narco-state or criminal state, which, being intertwined with organized crime, has no intention of undermining its own lucrative enterprises. Online betting serves both as a source of enormous revenue for public coffers and as a form of mass entertainment that distracts and pacifies the population. This “bread and circus” strategy operates by offering illusions to the poor and government employment to the middle class, thus securing passive support for increasingly authoritarian policies, including severe restrictions on freedom of expression and political dissent. Furthermore, the article denounces how the Brazilian judicial system actively suppresses public servants who attempt to apply the law impartially, punishing judges and prosecutors while protecting corrupt political elites. The result is a political environment where dissent is silenced, the state strengthens its control over society, and the financial, bureaucratic, and criminal sectors cooperate to sustain an oppressive regime",2025,Caixeta,OSF,10.17605/osf.io/9brhe,,https://doi.org/10.17605/osf.io/9brhe,und,datacite:Text/Project | openaire:Other literature type,datacite;openaire,2,False,True,False,,,,,
