R1700,Efecto de la carga tributaria del Impuesto a la Renta en la situación financiera de las empresas de apuestas en plataformas digitales en Ecuador,"La presente investigación examina cómo la carga tributaria del Impuesto a la Renta influye en la situación financiera de las empresas de apuestas digitales en Ecuador. Debido al continuo crecimiento de las apuestas en línea, el sector enfrenta retos fiscales y regulatorios. El objetivo principal de este estudio es evaluar el impacto de la carga tributaria en el rendimiento financiero de las plataformas de apuestas en Ecuador, centrado en el periodo 2019-2023. Se empleó un diseño no experimental de tipo cuantitativo, utilizando datos secundarios provenientes de la Superintendencia de Compañías, Valores y Seguros de Ecuador. A través de los datos financieros analizados, se encontró que los indicadores de liquidez muestran una caída significativa desde 2020, alcanzando niveles críticos en 2022 y 2023, lo que refleja serias dificultades para cubrir obligaciones a corto plazo. Por otro lado, los indicadores de solvencia evidencian un fuerte endeudamiento del patrimonio en 2023, aumentando el riesgo de insolvencia. Asimismo, la carga tributaria no depende directamente de los ingresos, y aunque algunas empresas presentan ingresos elevados, muchas de ellas registran pérdidas, evitando así el pago de impuestos. No obstante, se observó que esta carga tiene un efecto negativo en la rentabilidad del sector, lo que valida la hipótesis planteada. Entre las principales conclusiones, se resalta la necesidad de reforzar la regulación fiscal y mejorar el marco normativo para garantizar el cumplimiento de las normativas y la transparencia en el sector, asegurando un tratamiento justo para todas las empresas involucradas. The present research examines how the Income Tax burden influences the financial situation of digital betting companies in Ecuador. Due to the continuous growth of online betting, the sector faces fiscal and regulatory challenges. The main objective of this study is to evaluate the impact of the tax burden on the financial performance of betting platforms in Ecuador, focusing on the period 2019-2023. A non-experimental quantitative design was employed, using secondary data from the Superintendencia de Compañías, Valores y Seguros de Ecuador. Through the financial data analyzed, it was found that liquidity indicators have shown a significant decline since 2020, reaching critical levels in 2022 and 2023, reflecting serious difficulties in meeting shortterm obligations. On the other hand, solvency indicators reveal a strong increase in equity indebtedness in 2023, raising the risk of insolvency. Likewise, the tax burden does not directly depend on income, and although some companies report high revenues, many of them record losses, thus avoiding tax payments. Nonetheless, it was observed that this burden negatively affects the sector's profitability, validating the proposed hypothesis. Among the main conclusions, the need to strengthen tax regulation and improve the regulatory framework is highlighted to ensure compliance with tax regulations and transparency in the sector, ensuring fair treatment for all companies involved.",2025,Huayamave Bustos,,,,http://dspace.ups.edu.ec/handle/123456789/30438,spa,openaire:Bachelor thesis,openaire,1,False,True,False,,,,,
R1701,Towards harmonised online age verification? A comparative study of French and EU legal frameworks,,2025,Humain-Lescop,SSRN Electronic Journal,10.2139/ssrn.5123971,,https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.5123971,en,openalex:preprint,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R1702,Laws on The Management of the Underground Economy in the Criminal Sector in Vietnam,"This study explores the complex relationship between criminal law and the underground economy in Vietnam, highlighting both its economic contributions and its detrimental effects on social order, security, and individual well-being. The underground economy—comprising unregistered businesses, informal labor, and illicit trade—has persisted due to gaps in legal enforcement, economic inequality, and the pursuit of profit outside regulatory oversight. While it can stimulate short-term economic activity, it also undermines fiscal stability, erodes trust in public institutions, and exposes participants to significant risks. To analyze this phenomenon, the study employs a qualitative research method that integrates literature review, juridical-normative analysis, and case-based exploration. Legal documents, policy papers, and academic studies are examined to understand how Vietnamese criminal law addresses underground economic activities. In addition, expert interviews with legal scholars, law enforcement officers, and economists provide contextual insights into enforcement challenges and policy gaps. This qualitative approach allows for a nuanced understanding of how law and informal economic practices interact in real-world contexts, beyond mere statistical data. The findings reveal that Vietnam’s criminal law serves not only as a deterrent mechanism but also as a regulatory instrument that shapes economic behavior. However, enforcement remains inconsistent, and coordination among state institutions remains limited. The study concludes with policy recommendations to improve legal frameworks, strengthen institutional capacity, and promote public awareness to manage and gradually formalize the underground economy in Vietnam effectively. REFERENCES Channel 14.Vn Electronic Newspaper (2018). “The story of legalizing prostitution in 10 countries around the world: The country allows prostitution but restricts the purchase of sex”. Access source: https://kenh14.vn/ specializing 20180407163634065.chn, accessed date: February 15, 2025. Dao, X. H., Nguyen, V. H., & Nguyen, D. A. (2023). “Requirements and recommendations to ensure social security for people working in the informal economy sector in Vietnam”. Journal of Namibian Studies, Vol. 33 (2023): Special Issue 3, e-ISSN 2197-5523, Publication date: May-22-2023, DOI: https://doi.org/10.59670/jns.v33i.1970 , https://namibian-studies.com/index.php/JNS/article/view/1970 , p. 932. Department For Social Vices Prevention - Ministry Of Labor, War Invalids And Social Affairs (2020). “The fates of Japan's red light district during the pandemic”. Access source: http://pctnxh.molisa.gov.vn/default.aspx?page=news&do=detail&id= 2742, accessed date: February 25, 2025. Economichelp. (2019). “Underground Economy - definition, problems and causes”. Access source: https://www.economicshelp.org , accessed date: February 25, 2025. Friedrich, S., & Robert, K. (2004). “Shadow economies around the world: What do we khow?”. CESifo Working Paper NO. 1167, Category 1: Public finance, April 2004. Hung , N. V., Thinh , T. C., & Duy, N. D. (2022). Cooperative Group In Current Vietnamese Commercial Environment. International Journal of Professional Business Review, 7(6), e0509, Access source: https://doi.org/10.26668/businessreview/2022.v7i6.e509 , p. 01. Hung, N. V. (2023). “Characteristics of the underground economy in Vietnam”. Lex Humana (ISSN 2175-0947), 15(3), access source: https://seer.ucp.br/seer/index.php/LexHumana/article/view/2537 , p. 18. Le, C., And NGUYEN, T. L. (2014). “Death Penalty in Vietnam’s Criminal Code: To Retain or Reduce and Eventually Abolish?”. Vietnam National University Journal of Science, Vol. 33 No. 3. National Assembly. “Criminal Code 1999 (amended and supplemented in 2009)”. National Assembly. “Criminal Code 2015 (amended and supplemented in 2017)”. Nguyen Vinh Hung (editor 2021). “Civil issues: Theoretical - Procedure - Comment”, People's Publish Security Publishing House. Nguyen, N. C. (2022). “Commentary on offenses against economic management order in the 2015 Criminal Code, amended and supplemented in 2017. National Political Publishing House, Hanoi. Nguyen, V. H. (2019). “The impact of the underground economy on the economy, society, and law”. Journal of Economic Studies, 7 (03). Nguyen, V. H. (2023_1). “Underground economy in the context of the fourth industrial revolution”. Journal of Political Theory, No.13. Nguyen, V. H. (2023_2). “Law on the management of the underground economy in Vietnam”. Topic scientific research in level school, Vietnam National University, Hanoi, University of Law. Nguyen, V. H., Nguyen, L. T & Tran C. T. (2023). Laws on the management of the underground economy in the financial sector in Vietnam, Lex Humana. Vol. 15 No. 4 (2023), ISSN 2175-0947, Publication date: July 20, 2023, https://seer.ucp.br/seer/index.php/LexHumana/article/view/2737 , p. 241. Nguyen, Vinh. H. (2020). “Managing the type of ""underground economy"" in Vietnam today”. State Management Review, 299 (12), 1-8. Nhung, D. H., Hung, N. V., & Nhung, K. T. T. (2023). “Land use planning of industrial zones in Vietnam towards sustainable development and climate change response”. Lex Humana (ISSN 2175-0947), 15(2), 1-8. https://seer.ucp.br/seer/index.php/LexHumana/article/view/2598 , p. 549. Tien Phong Electronic Newspaper (2023). “Hanoi announced that it would not allow prostitution to resume on Tran Duy Hung Street”. Access source: https://tienphong.vn/ha-noi-cong-bo-khong-de- tai-hoat-dong-mai-dam-o-pho-tran-duy-hung-post1506587.tpo , accessed date: February 15, 2025. Vietnam Open Educational Resources (2017). “Underground Economy”. Access source: https://voer.edu.vn/m/kinh-te-ngam/0d88638b , accessed date: February 23, 2025. Vnexpress Electronic Newspaper (2022). “Internet prostitution marketing”. Access source: https://vnexpress.net/topic/tiep-thi-mai-dam-qua-mang-internet-18578, accessed date: February 26, 2025. Vov2 Electronic Newspaper (2022). “Online football betting may have to go to prison”. Access source: https://vov2.vov.vn/phap-luat/ca-do-bong-da-online-co-the -phai-di-tu-39075.vov2, accessed date: February 15, 2025. Zing New Electronic Newspaper (2022). “Prostitutes in Thailand claim their rights”. Access source: https://zingnews.vn/gai-mai-dam-o-thai-lan-doi-quyen-loi -post1337923.html, accessed date: February 24, 2025.",2025,Hung,JURNAL CITA HUKUM,10.15408/jch.v13i2.47271,,https://doi.org/10.15408/jch.v13i2.47271,und,openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle;Review,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
