R5467,Der Markt für Sportwetten in Deutschland – Eine Bestandsaufnahme zwischen Law and Economics,,2017,Konstantin,Publications of the UdS (Saarland University),10.22028/d291-30690,,https://doi.org/10.22028/d291-30690,de,openalex_non_en:other,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R5468,Športne stave kot način dolgoročnega investiranja,"Sports betting is very popular in today's world. In the eyes of most participants in the market of sports betting, it can be a quick way to earn money. This misconception arises from ignorance of the specificities of the sports betting market, which in turn leads to the fact that the majority of participants are losing in the long run. We assumed that a better knowledge of the sports betting market could have changed this and that is why we studied the sports betting market and presented the findings. We divided the master's thesis into the theoretical and empirical part. In the theoretical part, we defined sports betting as a knowledge game, derived from game theory and decision theory. We wanted to clarify the differences between knowledge games and coincidental games and present theoretical views on decision-making in situations of risk and uncertainty. We presented the sports betting market and defined its operations from an economic point of view. By studying the sports betting market, we found many similarities with the financial market, which led us to the hypothesis of an effective market. Based on this, we checked the sports betting market efficiency. We presented all three forms of the efficient market hypothesis, weak, medium strong and strong. In the empirical part, we checked the sports betting market efficiency in the NBA basketball league based on the presented characteristics of the sports betting market. We have found that, irrespective of some patterns which may suggest the opposite, the market is effective and that it was not possible to achieve positive returns on it. Furthermore, we checked the knowledge of the sports betting market with a questionnaire among a randomly selected part of active players. The analysis of the collected data confirmed our assumptions that participants in the market are poorly informed of it and are not aware of all the traps that the sports betting market contains. At the end, we summarized the findings of the theoretical and empirical work of the master's thesis and carried out a model of long-term investment in the sports betting market that we believe could in the long run yield positive returns. Športne stave so v današnjem svetu zelo popularne. V očeh večine udeležencev na trgu športnih stav predstavljajo lahko pot do hitrega zaslužka. To zmotno mišljenje izhaja predvsem iz nepoznavanja posebnosti trga športnih stav, kar posledično privede to tega, da večina udeležencev na trgu športnih stav dolgoročno izgublja. Domnevali smo, da bi boljše poznavanje trga športnih stav to lahko spremenilo, zato smo trg športnih stav preučili in ugotovitve predstavljamo. Magistrsko delo je razdeljeno na teoretični in empirični del. V teoretičnem delu športne stave opredeljujemo kot igre znanja, ki izhajajo iz teorije iger in teorije odločanja. Želeli smo pojasniti razlike med igrami znanja in igrami naključij ter predstaviti teoretične poglede na odločanje v razmerah tveganja in negotovosti. Predstavljamo trg športnih stav in njegovo delovanje opredeljujemo z ekonomskih vidikov. Pri raziskovanju trga športnih stav smo odkrili veliko podobnosti s finančnim trgom, ki so nas privedle do hipotez učinkovitega trga, na podlagi katerih smo preverjali učinkovitost trga športnih stav. V magistrskem delu predstavljamo vse tri oblike hipotez učinkovitega trga: šibko, srednje močno in močno. V empiričnem delu na podlagi predstavljenih lastnosti trga športnih stav preverjamo učinkovitost trga športnih stav v košarkarski ligi NBA. Ugotovili smo, da je trg, kljub nekaterim vzorcem, ki bi lahko namigovali na nasprotno, učinkovit in da na njem ni bilo mogoče dosegati pozitivnega donosa. Poleg tega smo med naključno izbranimi aktivnimi igralci na trgu športnih stav z anketnim vprašalnikom preverili poznavanje trga športnih stav. Analiza zbranih podatkov je potrdila naše domneve, da udeleženci na trgu športnih stav trg slabo poznajo in se ne zavedajo vseh pasti, ki jih trg športnih stav vsebuje. Na koncu povzemamo vse ugotovitve iz teoretičnega in empiričnega dela magistrskega dela ter predstavljamo model dolgoročnega investiranja na trgu športnih stav, ki bi po našem mnenju dolgoročno lahko prinašal pozitivni donos.",2017,Kristl,K. Kristl,,,https://dk.um.si/IzpisGradiva.php?id=68690,slv,openaire:Master thesis,openaire,1,False,True,False,,,,,
R5469,Webový systém pro podporu kurzového sázení,This thesis deals with the analysis of actual situation in the sphere of online betting and implements the web system for the support of activities which are connected to it. The first part of the thesis describes the procedures of obtaining all the needed information and requirements for the target group of users. Subsequently after using this acquired knowledge the new system is designed with the help of the object-orientated programming. At the end the result is the new designed system which is implemented by modern web tools in the leading position with the popular frameworks.,2017,Krula,Digital Repository (National Repository of Grey Literature),,,http://www.nusl.cz/ntk/nusl-431594,cs,openaire:Master thesis | openalex:dissertation,openalex;openaire,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R5470,A coordinated health communication campaign addressing casino and sports gambling among undergraduate students,"Research has outlined many negative effects of disordered gambling. While gambling disorder exists among all US sociodemographic groups, college students are particularly vulnerable. This study describes a health communication approach commonly studied in the intervention of college behaviors such as risky alcohol/substance use and sexual activity. Specifically, two health communication messages targeting casino and sports betting disordered gambling were distributed at a Midwestern US public research university, and central intercept techniques were utilized to collect quantitative and qualitative data assessing student reception. Results revealed females preferred the casino message more than males (U = 4696.50, p &lt; .05) and stated more often that the advertisement would appeal to friends (U = 4745.50, p &lt; .05). Individuals who lost more money than they intended to lose 1–2 times understood the message more than those persons who never gambled (U = 946.50, p &lt; .05) and those persons who never lost more than planned (U = 249.50, p &lt; .05). Students who first gambled at ages 16–18 liked the casino message less than those students who first gambled at 13–15 (U = 208.00, p &lt; .05) and the students who had never gambled (U = 1656.00, p &lt; .05). For the sports betting message, the only significant association was between students’ understanding of the advertisement and race/ethnicity (c2(5) = 14.095, p &lt; .05). Based on our findings, we suggest a health communication approach might be effective to raise awareness about gambling disorder among college students. We recommend researchers develop targeted materials with support of college administrators to deter disordered gambling.RésuméLa recherche a mis en relief de nombreux effets négatifs du jeu pathologique. Bien qu’on retrouve des problèmes de jeu dans tous les groupes sociodémographiques américains, les étudiants constituent une classe particulièrement vulnérable. Cette étude décrit une approche de communication sur la santé qui est couramment étudiée pour effectuer des interventions sur les comportements à risque observés dans les collèges et universités, tels que la consommation d’alcool ou de drogues et l’activité sexuelle. Plus précisément, on a distribué deux messages sur la santé ciblant les jeux de hasard et les jeux de paris sportifs dans une université de recherche publique du Midwest américain, et on a eu recours à des techniques centrales d’interview pour recueillir des données quantitatives et qualitatives évaluant la réception des messages par les étudiants. Les résultats ont révélé que les femmes ont préféré les messages du casino davantage que les hommes (U = 4696,50, p &lt;0,05) et ont plus souvent dit que l’annonce intéresserait les amis (U = 4745,50, p &lt;0,05). Les personnes qui ont perdu au jeu une à deux fois de plus que prévu ont davantage saisi le message que ceux qui n’ont jamais joué (U = 946,50, p &lt;0,05) et que ceux qui n’ont jamais perdu plus que prévu (U = 249,50, p &lt;0,05). Les étudiants qui ont joué pour la première fois entre 16 et 18 ans ont moins aimé le message du casino que les étudiants qui ont joué la première fois entre 13 et 15 ans (U = 208, p &lt;0,05) et que les étudiants qui n’avaient jamais joué (U = 1656, p &lt;0,05). Pour le message sur les paris sportifs, la seule association significative était celle entre la compréhension de l’annonce par les étudiants et la race/l’origine ethnique, c2 (5) = 14,095, p &lt; 0,05. Selon nos constatations, nous sommes d’avis qu’une approche de communication sur la santé pourrait être efficace pour sensibiliser les étudiants aux problèmes du jeu. Nous recommandons donc aux chercheurs de concevoir du matériel ciblé, avec le soutien des administrateurs de collèges et d’universités, pour dissuader les comportements de jeu pathologique.",2017,Kruse‐Diehr,Journal of Gambling Issues,10.4309/jgi.2018.37.4,,https://doi.org/10.4309/jgi.2018.37.4,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | openalex_non_en:article | s2:,openalex;openalex_non_en;s2;crossref;openaire,5,False,False,False,,R5471,,,
