R5901,Problem ovisnosti o klađenju — Sportske kladionice u Mostaru,"We are witnessing a rise in the number of gambling addicts from day to day. Fast living, poverty, unemployment, stress of various types and also misunderstandings are most certainly some of the causes of the increase in the numbers of persons who gamble on a daily basis. However, an increase in the number of betting shops evidently also contributes to the fact that even elementary school students have begun to gamble. This paper discusses sports betting shops in Mostar. Sadly, research has demonstrated that numerous sports betting shops are located in the vicinity of elementary schools, but also near secondary schools in particular. Furthermore, gambling affects life within the family — gambling addiction is one of the causes of the rise in the number of divorces. The paper opens discussion on this contemporary problem and prompts the reader to take a broader approach and also to accept greater responsibility in resolving it at various levels in society. Broj ovisnika o kocki svakodnevno se povećava. Brz način života, siromaštvo, nezaposlenost, različiti stresovi i nesporazumi sigurno su neki od uzroka povećanja broja osoba koje svakodnevno kockaju. Međutim, i broj kladionica pridonosi tomu da već i učenici osnovnih škola počinju kockati. U ovom se radu govori o sportskim kladionicama u Mostaru. Nažalost, istraživanjem se došlo do činjenice da su brojne sportske kladionice smještene u blizini osnovnih škola, a pogotovo srednjih. Zatim, kockanje utječe i na život obiteljī. Ovisnost o kocki jedan je od uzroka povećanja broja rastava. Ovaj rad otvara aktualno pitanje ovisnosti o klađenju te potiče da se ovoj problematici pristupi šire i odgovornije na različitim društvenim razinama.",2016,Skoko,Obnovljeni Život : časopis za filozofiju i religijske znanosti,,,https://hrcak.srce.hr/156791,hrv,openaire:Article; Review,openaire,1,False,True,False,,,,,
R5902,The Problem of Gambling Addiction — Sports Betting Shops in Mostar,,2016,Skoko,Obnovljeni život : časopis za filozofiju i religijske znanosti,,,,hr,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R5903,Optimization of a Fanduel Salary Cap League Fantasy Football Team.pdf,"One-day fantasy football leagues are becoming more popular each season and fantasy players are looking for any kind of advantage to win their leagues. One of these salary cap leagues is hosted by the website FanDuel. Fantasy Football team owners can improve their chances to win by selecting an optimized team based off the previous week’s statistics. Two methods were written in order to maximize the total points scored by a FanDuel roster with a salary cap constraint. We implemented MATLAB’s built-in genetic algorithm function to create an optimal lineup based on the projected points per game of each player, and reliable lineups based on the uncertainty of each player to achieve a minimum target score. The genetic algorithm proved to be the best gradient-free optimization method for this approach. Gradient-free methods will help fantasy football team owners select a roster that helps them select a roster each week that will maximize their points while not going over the allotted salary cap. The discussed optimization methods can easily be applied to other fantasy sport leagues with a salary cap.",2016,Smith,figshare,10.6084/m9.figshare.3172630,,https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.3172630,,datacite:JournalArticle/Journal contribution | datacite:Text/Journal contribution,datacite,1,False,True,True,,,,,
