R6642,Development of Judgment Criterion for Problem Gamblers in Sports Lottery,"To screen items and define boundary value for problem gamblers’judgment criterion,by Delphi Method,the feedback data of 23 experts were statistically analyzed in terms of authority,concentricity and coordination.A total sample of 2 426 lottery consumers was assessed.The conclusions show that by Delphi Method and item discrimination method,the problem gamblers’judgment criterion consists of 12 items and 5 factors(continued and repeated purchasing behavior,cognitive bias,loss of control,abstinence,actus reus).2) By sensitivity,specificity and Youden index analysis on morbid group and control group,it shows that 6 point is the best boundary value to define problem gambler.It means the cutoff point of the problem gamblers scale was 6.3) With the standard of psychological status as the criterion,the chi-square test indicates there exists significant difference(P 0.01) among problem gamblers and non-problem gamblers.4) The problem gamblers’judgment criterion has a relatively reliability and validity,which can be regarded as a research tool.",2013,Hai-chen,Beijing Tiyu Daxue xuebao,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
