R7203,An analysis of Affiliate Marketing of Japanese sports lottery,"Affiliate marketing strategy carried out to market sports lottery in Japan was analyzed in this article.The results prove that affiliate marketing strategy has succeeded in Japan and that affiliate marketing is applicable to sport lottery marketing.In order to improve competitiveness and the healthy development of the Chinese sports lottery,the present paper suggests that affiliate marketing strategy can be adapted to marketing Chinese sports lottery.",2011,Hui,Liaoning tiyu ke-ji,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7204,Research on sustainable development of China's lottery industry based on the Hotelling model,"Lottery, as a source of government revenue, has played an important role in the development of public welfare. However, under the current issuing framework, Welfare Centre and the Sports Lottery Centre are in the price competition for market share. On the one hand, the raising efforts of Community Chest is weakened, on the other hand, public property of the lottery is damaged. So there is a urgent problem need to be solved that how does the financial authority coordinate the two major lottery centers by laying sales outlets. Through the extension analysis of Hotelling model this problem is discussed in depth and some conclusion is provided for competent authorities to develop the appropriate policies. The conclusions are following: when there is no difference in the lottery, the sales outlets should be placed far away from each other to avoid cannibalism; However, in order to maximize the total social profits, Welfare Lottery and Sports Lottery should strive to be competitive differentiation. When the two kinds of lottery are different, whether the lottery sales outlets is concentrated or discrete, the social gross profit is greater than there is no difference between the two kinds of lottery. This electronic document is a “live” template. The various components of your paper [title, text, heads, etc.] are already defined on the style sheet, as illustrated by the portions given in this document.",2011,Huihui,2011 International Conference on Business Management and Electronic Information,10.1109/icbmei.2011.5920472,,https://doi.org/10.1109/icbmei.2011.5920472,en,openaire:Article | openalex:conference-paper | s2:Conference,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R7205,Online Sports Betting and International Relations,"��� Sports gambling represents a universal past time in countries around the world, and the advent of online gambling has raised major issues of national sovereignty in the regulation of legal sports betting. Recent disputes between countries like the United States (US-Gambling) and Portugal (Liga Portuguesa) and online gambling operators in offshore jurisdictions have demonstrated the need for international legal agreements on these issues. An existing international betting system for horse races around the world offers one potential model as countries begin to consider a new legal regime for international online gambling.",2011,Humphreys,The SAIS review of international affairs,10.1353/sais.2011.0009,,https://doi.org/10.1353/sais.2011.0009,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R7206,Market Inefficiency and the Learning Curve: The Case of the Sports Lottery Market,"I document market inefficiency in the sports lottery market and examine how participants learn from such inefficiency. Using a novel, parimutuel type sports lottery data in Korea, I show that participants underbet certain outcomes relative to their realized probability. The magnitude of this bias is so great that a naive betting strategy of blindly betting on these outcomes, since the sports lottery's inception in 2008 through 2010, would have resulted in an average after-tax return that was greater than 75% for each game. The size of the abnormal return is even more surprising because these sports lotteries have an unconditional expected return of less than -50% due to a low payout rate. There is some evidence of the learning behavior of participants over time, but not enough to eliminate the above bias.",2011,Hwang,SSRN Electronic Journal,10.2139/ssrn.1787903,,https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.1787903,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article; Other literature type | openalex:preprint | s2:,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R7207,"Operation, Problems and the Impact of Chance Games on the Development of Sport in Slovenia","This Book looks at the Law and the Policy on Betting and Sport in many countries around the world—sport is a global phenomenon—providing a very useful and valuable comparative survey on a subject that is so vital to safeguarding and preserving the integrity of those sports in which betting is legally allowed. The country reports show how sports-related betting is organized in the country concerned, also from a historical and policy perspective (national Lotteries Act; state run/state licensed lotteries and/or private operators; how the licensing system for public operators works; state supervisory mechanisms, etc.), and contain a treatment of the national case-law. These keywords were added by machine and not by the authors. This process is experimental and the keywords may be updated as the learning algorithm improves.",2011,Jagodic,ASSER international sports law series,10.1007/978-90-6704-799-9_44,,https://doi.org/10.1007/978-90-6704-799-9_44,en,openalex:book-chapter | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
