R7485,The Efficiency of ‘In-Play’ Australian Rules Football Betting Markets,"This paper examines the efficiency of the “in-play” Australian Rules football fixed odds betting market at quarter time, half time, and three quarter time. Tests of semistrong efficiency are performed on the 2009 AFL season using logistic regression analysis. The results demonstrate that as the match progresses, there is a significant bias against the team that is currently leading—a bias that increases when the team that is leading is also the away-favorite. This bias is shown to yield significant profits utilizing simple betting strategies.",2010,Ryall,International Journal of Sport Finance,10.1177/155862351000500303,,https://doi.org/10.1177/155862351000500303,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R7486,"Palabras de salutación en la presentación del libro ""Las apuestas deportivas""",,2010,Sampedro,Revista Aranzadi de derecho de deporte y entretenimiento,,,,es,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7487,Statistics and sportsbook,"This bachelor thesis describes the history and fundamental terminology of sportsbook. In theoretical part it describes how to become successful bookmaker and explains specific procedures. In practical part are these procedures applied to real outputs and there's given a solution how to process analysis of sportsbook on the rebound. There are further analysed the lottery and betting games as a complex unit, in which it's finding specific trend and it also deals with the return rate in single games. The last part of the thesis describes frequency testing of relative hypotheses, which are based on favorite betting analysis. During this testing there is compared this frequency in individual seasons and also in a single season.",2010,Schatral,Digital Repository (National Repository of Grey Literature),,,,cs,openalex:dissertation,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7488,Better Odds for Sports Betting,,2010,Schneider,Gaming Law Review and Economics,10.1089/glre.2010.14706,,https://doi.org/10.1089/glre.2010.14706,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R7489,Auf der Ebene eines Bundeslands bestehendes staatliches Monopol auf die Veranstaltung von Sportwetten; Unvereinbarkeit der ein solches Monopol betreffenden Regelung mit dem dt Grundgesetz; Zulässigkeit und eventuelle Voraussetzungen einer Übergangszeit,"Aufgrund des Vorrangs des unmittelbar geltenden Unionsrechts darf eine nationale Regelung über ein staatliches Sportwettenmonopol, die nach den Feststellungen eines nationalen Gerichts Beschränkungen mit sich bringt, die mit der Niederlassungsfreiheit und dem freien Dienstleistungsverkehr unvereinbar sind, weil sie nicht dazu beitragen, die Wetttätigkeiten in kohärenter und systematischer Weise zu begrenzen, nicht für eine Übergangszeit weiter angewandt werden.",2010,Schuhmacher,Wirtschaftsrechtliche Blätter,10.1007/s00718-010-1726-y,,https://doi.org/10.1007/s00718-010-1726-y,de,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7490,"Not Undertaking the Almost-Impossible Task: The 1961 Wire Act's Development, Initial Applications, and Ultimate Purpose","For a Camelot-era piece of legislation, the Wire Act has a long and unintended shadow. Used haltingly in the 1960s, when the Wire Act failed to deliver the death blow to organized crime, 1970â€™s Racketeer-Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (RICO) became a far better weapon against the mob. Yet starting in the 1990s, the Wire Act enjoyed a second life, when the Justice Department used to it prosecute operators of online betting Web sites that, headquartered in jurisdictions where such businesses were legal, took bets from American citizens. The legislative history of the Wire Act, however, suggests that it was intended for a much more selective application, and that the use of the Act to penalize those who provide cross-border betting services to Americans, while perhaps faithful to the broad letter of the Act, is a departure from its spirit. Analyzing the social and political ferment in which the Wire Act and its companion laws were brewed shows that the entire package of ostensibly anti-gambling legislation passed by Congress in the summer of 1961 was actually an anti-organized crime measure that only attacked purveyors of gambling because of their important position in the organized crime chain of command. It was not then intended as a sweeping federal effort to curtail public access to gambling. Further, the fact that the same committee in which the attorney general received his initial education in organized crime proposed, in the following year, an expansion of the Act to cover technologies not specified in the original law, suggests that the Wire Act was intended to cover only a limited range of wire facilitiesâ€”not the broad spectrum of communications technologies, most of which had not yet been invented in 1961, for which later prosecutors dusted it off.",2010,Schwartz,Gaming Law Review and Economics,10.1089/glre.2010.14708,,https://doi.org/10.1089/glre.2010.14708,en,openaire:Article | openalex:article,openalex;openaire,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7491,Optimiser la présence d'un site sur internet : le cas des sites de paris en ligne,"Si le marche des jeux en ligne s'est officiellement ouvert en France le 8 juin 2010, cela fait de nombreuses annees qu'il existe de facon officieuse pour les internautes francais. Les paris en ligne sont sources de toutes les convoitises depuis bien des annees. Les bookmakers, qui proposent aux joueurs de parier sur de nombreuses rencontres sportives, ont rapidement compris a quel point ce marche pouvait prendre de l'ampleur avec la legalisation des jeux d'argent en ligne. Depuis le debut de l'ete, ils inondent les medias de publicites pour parier sur le sport ou jouer au poker. Et il n'y a pas que les operateurs qui profitent des retombees mediatiques. Tout l'univers des jeux en ligne est concerne par cette legalisation et les sites de conseils en paris sportifs ou poker en profitent pour accroitre le nombre de leurs visiteurs. Voici en quelques mots le contexte dans lequel je suis amenee a faire mon stage.",2010,Seguillon,HAL (Le Centre pour la Communication Scientifique Directe),,,,fr,openalex_non_en:dissertation,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7492,Your Mother Should Know: A Comparison of Maternal and Paternal Attitudes and Behaviors Related to Gambling among Their Adolescent Children,,2010,Shead,International Journal of Mental Health and Addiction,10.1007/s11469-010-9279-0,,https://doi.org/10.1007/s11469-010-9279-0,en,openalex:article | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7493,The Legal Regulation of Sports Betting in Germany,"Sports betting is very popular in Germany.Although it is legal,the state-run corporation monopoly and internet betting ban over sports betting often led to match fixing scandal.In spite of the fact that European Union law and European Court of Justice's awards are binding to Germany,EU members can make their own sports betting laws and regulations,including Germany.",2010,Shi-xi,Journal of Sports Sciences,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7494,Are Crowds Wise When Predicting Against Point Spreads? It Depends on How You Ask,,2010,Simmons,,,,,,s2:,s2,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7495,Intuitive Biases in Choice versus Estimation: Implications for the Wisdom of Crowds,"Although researchers have documented many instances of crowd wisdom, it is important to know whether some kinds of judgments may lead the crowd astray, whether crowds’ judgments improve with feedback over time, and whether crowds’ judgments can be improved by changing the way judgments are elicited. We investigated these questions in a sports gambling context (predictions against point spreads) believed to elicit crowd wisdom. In a season-long experiment, fans wagered over $20,000 on NFL football predictions. Contrary to the wisdom-of-crowds hypothesis, faulty intuitions led the crowd to predict “favorites” more than “underdogs” against point spreads that disadvantaged favorites, even when bettors knew that the spreads disadvantaged favorites. Moreover, the bias increased over time, a result consistent with attributions for success and failure that rewarded intuitive choosing. However, when the crowd predicted game outcomes by estimating point differentials rather than by predicting against point spreads, its predictions were unbiased and wiser.",2010,Simmons,Journal of Consumer Research,10.1086/658070,,https://doi.org/10.1086/658070,en,datacite:JournalArticle/Journal contribution | openaire:Article; Other literature type | openalex:article,openalex;datacite;openaire,3,False,False,False,,R6202,,,
R7496,SOCL 266 - Sport and Society,"Course Description Sport and society is a course in the sociology of sport. Perhaps the most compelling reason for the sociological study of sport is its pervasiveness. Sport sociologist D. Stanley Eitzen suggests just how pervasive it is in American society (Fair and Foul, 2nd ed., pp. 3-4): Participation rates are high. Most children are involved in organized sport at some time in their lives. Sport is the subject of much conversation, reading material, leisure activity, and discretionary spending. Over one-tenth of the World Almanac is devoted annually to sport, more than is allotted to politics, business, and science. USA Today, the most widely read newspaper in the United States, devotes one-fourth of its space to sport. Even the Wall Street Journal has a weekly sports page. Several cable television networks provide twenty-four-hour coverage. Almost one-fifth of major network time is devoted to sport. Annually, the most watched television event in the United States is the Super Bowl. The amount of sports betting is staggering, with unknown billions waged legally and illegally. As Eitzen further points out, sports fans know a great deal about sports from following their favorite teams and athletes in the media. They know about point spreads, statistics, and biographical information on athletes and coaches. As children, many of us learned sports information, memorizing incredible amounts of trivia. Moreover, most of us play sports, as individuals or on teams, throughout our lives. Yet many fans and participants have a superficial, uncritical attitude toward sport. They cannot separate the hype from the reality. They don’t question the way that sport is organized. Sociologists are prone to examine all social arrangements critically. Thus, this course will address questions such as: How does sport really work? Who has power and who does not? Who benefits under the existing social arrangements and who does not? These types of questions scrutinize conventional ideas and official dogma; the answers should enable you to truly understand sports as social phenomena.",2010,Singleton,TRAILS: Teaching Resources and Innovations Library for Sociology,,,,en,openalex:article,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7497,Competitiveness and efficiency of online sport betting markets : an empirical approach [Top Thesis],,2010,Staniszewski,,,,,,s2:,s2,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7498,Vývojová studie fungování a vlivu sázkových kanceláří ve sportovním prostředí,"Title: Developmental study of functioning and influence of betting offices in sports environment. Goal: Charting the history of gambling and betting offices, based on historical and legislative documents. Methods: Descriptive analysis, Developmental study, Interview. Results: Assessment of the development form of sports betting and prediction of its future role within the sports scene. Keywords: Sports betting, gambling, betting offices, lottery law, developmental study, descriptive analysis, interview. 3",2010,Statečný,,,,http://www.nusl.cz/ntk/nusl-276534,ces/cze,openaire:Master thesis,openaire,1,False,True,False,,,,,
R7499,Developmental study of functioning and influence of betting offices in sports environment.,"Title: Developmental study of functioning and influence of betting offices in sports environment. Goal: Charting the history of gambling and betting offices, based on historical and legislative documents. Methods: Descriptive analysis, Developmental study, Interview. Results: Assessment of the development form of sports betting and prediction of its future role within the sports scene. Keywords: Sports betting, gambling, betting offices, lottery law, developmental study, descriptive analysis, interview. 3",2010,Statečný,Digital Repository (National Repository of Grey Literature),,,,cs,openalex:dissertation,openalex,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7500,Issues in sports forecasting,"Abstract A large amount of effort is spent on forecasting the outcomes of sporting events, but few papers have focused exclusively on the characteristics of sports forecasts. Instead, many papers have been written about the efficiency of sports betting markets. As it turns out, it is possible to derive a considerable amount of information about the forecasts and the forecasting process from studies that have tested the markets for economic efficiency. Moreover, the huge number of observations provided by betting markets makes it possible to obtain robust tests of various forecasting hypotheses. This paper is concerned with a number of forecasting topics in horse racing and several team sports. The first topic involves the type of forecast that is made: picking a winner or predicting whether a particular team will beat the point spread. Different evaluation procedures will be examined and alternative forecasting methods (models, experts, and the market) compared. The paper also examines the evidence with regard to the existence of biases in the forecasts, and concludes by discussing the applicability of these results to forecasting in general.",2010,Stekler,International Journal of Forecasting,10.1016/j.ijforecast.2010.01.003,,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijforecast.2010.01.003,en,openaire:Article; Preprint | openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R7501,Examining the psychological factors associated with fantasy sports participants,,2010,Suh,,,,,,s2:,s2,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7502,Examining the psychological factors associated with involvement in fantasy sports: An analysis of participants’ motivations and constraints,"This study examined how fantasy sport participants’ motives and constraints influence their attitudes toward fantasy sports participation. Furthermore, the study attempted to develop a reliable and valid model through which researchers can measure fantasy sports participation-related motivations and constraints. The proposed model for motivations consisted of 21 items with seven dimensions (i.e., economic, social interaction, escape, fantasy, achievement, knowledge, and pass time) and the model for constraints consisted of 15 items with five dimensions (i.e., time, accessibility, lack of interest, lack of partners, and lack of knowledge) for fantasy sports participants. The Structural Equation Modeling (SEM) method with a convenience sample of 161 participants was employed to analyze the conceptual framework and psychometric property of the scale. Motivations for fantasy sports participants were positively and significantly related to and constraints for fantasy sports participants were negatively and significantly related to their attitude toward fantasy sports participation. These results and future implications for practical and theoretical research are also discussed.",2010,Suh,International Journal of Sport Management Recreation & Tourism,10.5199/ijsmart-1791-874x-5a,,https://doi.org/10.5199/ijsmart-1791-874x-5a,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article; Other literature type | openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R7503,"Participants’ Service Quality Perceptions of Fantasy Sports Websites: The Relationship between Service Quality, Customer Satisfaction, Attitude, and Actual Usage","The purpose of this study was to examine participants’ perceptions of the service quality of fantasy sports websites and to understand the relationship between service quality, satisfaction, attitude, and actual usage associated with the websites. Furthermore, this study compared the proposed service-quality model with a rival model to examine the role of satisfaction and attitude as mediating variables. The proposed service-quality measure consisted of four perceived service quality dimensions (i.e., ease of use, trust, content, and appearance). A convenience sample of 279 participants was collected from message board users of four fantasy sports websites (i.e., ESPN.com Fantasy Games, Yahoo! Fantasy Sports, FOX Fantasy Sports, and NFL Events: Fantasy Sports). Structural analysis revealed that satisfaction and attitude acted as mediating variables connecting service quality and actual usage of fantasy sports websites. These results are discussed and the study's theoretical and practical sport marketing implications are detailed.",2010,Suh,Sport Marketing Quarterly,10.1177/106169341001900203,,https://doi.org/10.1177/106169341001900203,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:JournalArticle,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R7504,Present state and tasks of the sport lottery ticket in China,,2010,Sun,神戸大学大学院人間発達環境学研究科研究紀要,,,,ja,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7505,A Study on the Problems and Countermeasures of Sports Lotteries in China,,2010,Tang,,,,,,s2:,s2,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7506,Behavioral Economics Analysis on Product Design of Sports Lottery,"This paper studies behavioral economics of sports lottery product considering three kinds of conditions including single item of reward, multi-item of reward with equal number and multi-item of reward with increasing number based on cumulative prospect theory. The study indicates that the price for sports lottery increases and the total funds raised increases as the items increasing, and the pricing for sports lottery under multi-item of reward with increasing number condition is very reasonable. The proposed research on the designing and pricing of sports lottery product is of theoretical meaning as well as referential value.",2010,Tang,"International Conference on Information Management, Innovation Management and Industrial Engineering (ICIII)",10.1109/iciii.2010.486,,https://doi.org/10.1109/iciii.2010.486,en,crossref:proceedings-article | openaire:Article | openalex:conference-paper | s2:Conference,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R7507,Gambling in Brazil: Lifetime prevalences and socio-demographic correlates,,2010,Tavares,Psychiatry Research,10.1016/j.psychres.2010.04.014,20483469,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psychres.2010.04.014,en,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,reference of Tran 2024,,,,
R7508,Las apuestas deportivas en Euskadi,,2010,Unzalu,Dialnet (Universidad de la Rioja),,,,es,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7509,Towards a B2B Model for Online Gambling Operators in Belgium: Is the New Business Model Viable for all Stakeholders?,"On December 3, 2009 the Lower Chamber of the Belgian Parliament adopted the New Belgian Gaming Legislation (hereinafter referred to as the “Gaming Law”). The Gaming Law has been passed without any substantial amendments, notwithstanding the EU Commission’s objections with regard to some of the core provisions of the Gaming Law. The Gaming Law has been published in the Belgian Official Gazette on February 1, 2010: it should enter into force by January 1, 2011 at the latest, although Implementing Regulations (Royal Decrees of Execution) may provide for some provisions to enter into force earlier. The latter option seems highly unlikely to materialize since the Belgian Government has resigned and parliamentary elections have been held on June 13… This contribution will briefly discuss both the Gaming Law’s main features and the current regulatory framework with respect to sports betting (whether fixed-odd or mutual) and will draw some conclusions as regards the Gaming Law’s application to new entrants on the Belgian online sports betting market.",2010,Verbiest,Gaming Law Review and Economics,10.1089/glre.2010.14803,,https://doi.org/10.1089/glre.2010.14803,eng,openaire:Article | s2:JournalArticle,s2;openaire,2,False,False,False,,R7245,,,
R7510,Gambling Regulation and Risk,"This section discusses the regulation of “lifestyle risks”, a term that can apply to both substances and behaviours. Lifestyle risks take place along the line of “abstinence – consumption – abuse – addiction”. This can concern substances such as food, alcohol or drugs, as well as behaviours such as gambling or sports. The section also addresses the question of the appropriate point of equilibrium between free choice and state intervention (regulation), as well as the question of when risks can be considered to be acceptable or tolerable. In line with the interdisciplinary scope of the journal, the section aims at updating readers on both the regulatory and the scientific developments in the field. It analyses legislative initiatives and judicial decisions and at the same time it provides insight into recent empirical studies on lifestyle risks.",2010,Villeneuve,European Journal of Risk Regulation,10.1017/s1867299x00000878,,https://doi.org/10.1017/s1867299x00000878,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7511,Creación de modelos de predicción orientados a las apuestas de eventos deportivos,"El estudio expuesto en este documento lleva a cabo un proceso de descubrimiento de conocimiento mediante técnicas de inteligencia artificial en el dominio de las apuestas en eventos deportivos. En concreto el estudio se centra en el tenis masculino e individual. Para realizar dicho estudio se siguió la metodología CRISP-DM y se tuvieron como principales objetivos los siguientes: Aplicar distintas técnicas de minería de datos, para analizar el gran volumen de datos disponible de tenistas, sus partidos y los movimientos que estos generan en el mercado de las apuestas deportivas. Conocer qué factores son más determinantes en un partido de tenis y en su resultado final. Conocer el movimiento de las apuestas de un partido de tenis y analizar si este conocimiento puede ser útil para una posible inversión en las apuestas. Diseñar un sistema automático mediante el cual se consiga maximizar la ganancia de una posible inversión en apuestas deportivas gracias al conocimiento extraído en la predicción de partidos de tenis y del movimiento de las apuestas.",2010,Vivar Angulo,,,,https://hdl.handle.net/10016/10361,esl/spa,openaire:Master thesis; Other literature type,openaire,1,False,True,False,,,,,
R7512,Understanding the impact of gambling with special reference to Thailand,"This thesis mainly consists of three empirical chapters related to understanding the characteristics, economic impact and the demand for gambling in Thailand. Beginning with a review of the theoretical and empirical literature, this confirms that socio-economic and demographic data are important determinants of the level of gambling participation and gambling expenditure. A Logit model is then used to estimate the participation of gambling. The results suggest that the number games, such as the government lottery, the underground lottery, are popular among old gamblers whereas football betting is popular for adolescents. In the past, most casino customers were old gamblers, but at present the number of young gamblers who participate in casino has considerably increased. A Tobit model is employed to estimate the level of gambling frequency and gambling expenditure. The estimations reveal that there is a “supplementation effect” of casino on other gambling types and the effect also appears among the number games. The gambling expenditures on the number games are high in the group of gamblers who have undergraduate degree or lower while the expenditures on casino and football betting are high in the group of gamblers who have undergraduate degree. However, a higher education level leads to a lower level of gambling expenditures. The focus is then centred on the 2-3 digit lottery. The rational addiction model is tested for the case of the 2-3 digit lottery. In the addiction framework, the 2-3 digit lottery is found to be an addictive goods and the addiction is “myopic addiction”. This finding is confirmed by Instrumental Variable estimation.",2010,Vongsinsirikul,University of Birmingham Institutional Research Archive (University of Birmingham),,,,en,openalex:dissertation | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7513,Fantasy Sports: The Road to Information Literacy Championships,,2010,Waelchli,,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7514,A Research on the Slow Development of Sports Industry in the Primary Level of Under-developed Areas,"Sports industry is an important content of economic development and social progress for a country or area.By means of literature review,interviews with experts and questionnaire,the authors of this text have surveyed the current situation of sports industry development in the primary level of under-developed areas and established a system of evaluation index,and based on this,they have carried on vertical and horizontal comparison to evaluate the developing process of sports industry,in the attempt to offer scientific consultation for the development of sports industry in the primary level of under-developed areas.The results show:1) the development of sports industry in the primary level of under-developed areas is still at the starting stage because of the relatively poor basic conditions and sports industry in the areas has not formed any scale and yet to be fostered further;2) the development of sports industry mainly depends on the fund-raising by sales of sports lottery ticket and shop-leasing in the primary level of under-developed areas,while sports fitness and recreation facility,sports competition and shows,sports technical training and the building of sports gymnasiums and stadiums have not been developed well,and as a result,its self-developing function is not established;3) there are not any comprehensive developing policies of sports industry in the under-developed areas,the sports operation service and projects that may attract sports investment,offered by the local government are quite limited.Besides,the sports consumption idea of the common people has not been totally formed,the sports industry invested by social forces develops slowly and the sports market has not taken shape yet.",2010,Wan-ling,Journal of Capital Institute of Physical Education,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7515,A brief analysis on the developing opportunity of the 12th National Games bring to Liaoning sports industry,"In 2013,Liaonig province will undertake the 12th National Games,which will provide some distinct opportunities for Liaoning province's sports industry as follow:the proportions of fitness and entertainment,competitive preferment in the whole sports industry will be further raised and developed;industrial subjects of the sports lottery will be improved in large scale,and the sports industrial structure will be further revised and optimized.",2010,Wang,Liaoning tiyu ke-ji,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7516,"Profit-Making Mechanism in ""Sports Lottery with 3""","This paper analyzed the mechanism of profit-making in lottery with 3 through statistical theory for a better understanding of sports lottery based on statistics.Based on expectancy and the law of large numbers and integrated fruit,it explained why Sports Lottery Management Centre could make profit in lottery with 3.",2010,Wang,Journal of Hebei Institute of Physical Education,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7517,Study on the Attitude toward the Sports Gambling among Citizens in Shanghai,"From Sports Lottery's attitude and personality trait questionnaires,coming from 1800 people in Shanghai.It analyzed the feature of different groups about sports betting attitudes,explored the relationship between Sports Lottery's attitude and personality trait.The result showed the public awareness of sports betting is more rational,emotion tends to positive,the attitude toward buying behavior tends to avoid,the attitude of sports gamble is different in sex,age,educated level and other variables and personality traits are closely related.",2010,Wang,Sichuan Sports Science,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7518,Bettor (Ir-)Rationality: Evidence of Observational Learning in an Online Betting Market,"We empirically examine the dynamics of an online voting market with long time horizons using a unique data set covering all publicly visible activity for one particular voting market for the period 2003-2009. Specifically, we draw on observational learning to infer the extent of agent irrationality. This preliminary work establishes that the market indeed shows some signs of observational learning, and given this we establish bounds on the likelihood of herding. Given the unique market structure of our research setting we assert our findings to represent a “worst case” scenario with regards to the potential for market herding. Our work contributes to a nascent stream of research examining long-run prediction market dynamics.",2010,Ward,SSRN Electronic Journal,,,,en,openalex:preprint | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7519,Online Fantasy Sports Litigation and the Need for a Federal Right of Publicity Statute,"The right of publicity is currently a jumble of state common law and state statutes, but the online fantasy sports industry crosses state lines with ease. Having witnessed the great revenue potential of online fantasy sports, professional sports leagues are trying to strong-arm independent fantasy sports providers out of the business by using the right of publicity to assert property interests in the statistics generated by professional players, and used by fantasy sports providers to run their online games. The first such attempt--by Major League Baseball--failed. However, the state law nature of the right of publicity prevents any single court opinion from binding the industry or other jurisdictions. The National Football League is attempting to achieve a more favorable result in a different jurisdiction. If successful, other professional sports leagues will be encouraged to litigate the issue, and Major League Baseball might even attempt to re-litigate its position in other states. This free-for-all could result in different rules for different sports in different states, which would not only be untenable for the online fantasy sports providers, but a violation of the Constitution as well. A cohesive federal right of publicity statute would (1) bring uniformity to the doctrine, (2) give federal courts (where these actions are being brought) a federal law to apply instead of allowing them to continue muddying the application of state laws, (3) directly address First Amendment concerns, and (4) solve the dormant commerce clause violation alluded to above.",2010,Weaver,Duke Law Scholarship Repository (Duke University),,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7520,Detection of impulse control disorders in Parkinson disease patients.,,2010,Weiss,The Neurologist,10.1097/nrl.0b013e3181e8868b,21150395,https://doi.org/10.1097/nrl.0b013e3181e8868b,,s2:LettersAndComments;Review,s2,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7521,Gambling habits of athletes and nonathletes classified as disordered gamblers.,"The objective of the present study was to determine the forms of gambling that were the most prevalent in those having problems with their gambling. High-risk individuals who were experiencing difficulties with their gambling were examined. Specifically, the gambling behaviors of current athletes, former athletes, and nonathletes were investigated. Only members of these 3 groups with elevated scores on the South Oaks Gambling Screen (SOGS) were tested. Specifically, only those classified as disordered gamblers (SOGS score > or = 3) were recruited. Among these individuals with high SOGS scores, former athletes were more likely to participate in skill-based forms of gambling such as sports gambling and poker card playing, whereas nonathletes were more likely to partake in gambling games that were based predominately on chance factors. Also, former athletes were more likely to wager on the sport they had once played. Findings suggest that a competitive spirit may lead athletes to involvement in skill-based forms of gambling. While other explanations were considered, preliminary indicators support this view.",2010,Weiss,The Journal of psychology,10.1080/00223980.2010.503248,21053765,https://doi.org/10.1080/00223980.2010.503248,eng,europepmc:Journal Article|src=MED | openaire:Article | openalex:article | pubmed:Journal Article | s2:JournalArticle,pubmed;europepmc;openalex;s2;openaire,5,False,False,False,,,,,
R7522,Gambling and Problem Gambling Across the Lifespan,,2010,Welte,Journal of Gambling Studies,10.1007/s10899-010-9195-z,20499144,https://doi.org/10.1007/s10899-010-9195-z,en,citations:article,citations,1,True,False,False,reference of Tran 2024,,,,
R7523,The Cognition Bias of the Consumer in the Sports Lottery Based on the Behavioral Economics,"Cognitive bias has been regarded as a universal phenomenon in the consumption of sports lottery.The adverse effects of such bias included its affections to both healthy developments of the lottery industry and social stability.The authors investigated cognitive bias phenomenon such as intuitive bias,mental accounting,sunk cost effect,emotional and social interaction and self-control phenomena from the perspective of behavioral economics,combining with relevant researches in finance and psychology,and further discussed the corresponding corrective strategies and possible future research directions.",2010,Wen-fei,,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7524,China's Sports Lottery Network Operation,"Analyzing the systematic structure of China's sports lottery operation,the paper focuses on the characteristics,status quo and existing problems of the network operation model of China's sports lottery and sets forth some measures and suggestions for solving the problems.",2010,Wen-ke,Sport Science Research,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7525,Momentum and Sports Betting,"I document that momentum trading strategies are significantly profitable in an intragame NBA sports betting market. The momentum profits appear to be the result of market underreaction to news, but I find no evidence that the underreaction is driven by the psychological biases that form the foundation of existing behavioral models of momentum. Together, my results suggest that new theories of momentum might be needed.",2010,Williams,Elsevier BV,10.2139/ssrn.1553150,,https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.1553150,en,crossref:posted-content | openaire:Article; Other literature type | openalex:preprint,openalex;crossref;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R7527,Market efficiency and the NHL totals betting market: Is there an under bias?,Sports betting and racetrack markets continue to be utilized by academic researchers to provide insights into theories relating to more complex speculative markets. Previous investigations have focused on testing the efficient markets hypotheses and behavioral biases of the participants. This paper investigates the market efficiency of the National Hockey League (NHL) goal totals over/under betting market. The market is found to be inefficient and simple wagering strategies are identified that result in profitable returns.,2010,Woodland,Economics bulletin,,,http://www.accessecon.com/Pubs/EB/2010/Volume30/EB-10-V30-I4-P287.pdf,en,openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R7528,The Present Situation of Sports Industry's Legislation in China,,2010,Xiao,,,,,,s2:Review,s2,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7529,Research of Mobile Lottery System,"Mobile lottery system integration of wireless networks and mobile communication advantages of electronic betting systems using the widely used mobile communication terminal,so Lottery from the traditional paper lottery buying patterns,for the lottery opened up a broader market space provides a practical solution program.This view of the current sports lottery,welfare lottery actively promote the mobile lottery business,based on Web Services technology,combined with the current system of many wince embedded devices,using the C # programming language and embedded database SQLITE in the framework of 3G mobile technology is designed mobile lottery system.",2010,Ya-xiong,Computer Knowledge and Technology,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7530,Analysis on the Current Situation of Sports Gambling Researches in China and Foreign Countries,"The present paper reviewed the major researches in sports gambling in China and foreign countries.The results show that Chinese scholars mainly focus on such areas as development strategies,markets,basic theories of sports lottery,consumers,management and legal problems,while their overseas counterparts mainly concern the social responsibility of sports gambling,teenager gambling and gambling psychology,giving priority to social benefits and economic benefits.After the analysis of the current situation of sports gambling in China and foreign countries,it pointed out that the future sports gambling researches in China should give more attention to the social responsibility of gambling and strengthen gambling research.",2010,Yan,Shanghai Tiyu Xueyuan xuebao,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7531,Criminal Regulations on Preventing Football Gambling,"From the angle of startup of criminal justice procedures, there are a lot of gambling models in football, such as pure footballs gambling via internet and gambling over controlling the football match. The commonness of the pure gambling and the specialty of the controlling match results require to set up the quick intervention mechanism of justices during preventing football gambling. The essence of football gambling crime beyond the mass organizations punishment asks for the initiative of justice intervention. For the characteristic of common crime and special crime, it is required that forensics must be finished by multi-cooperation. From the angle of application of criminal law, the present regulations can rule the crime acts of gambling, but from the angle of behavior criminal law, the creation of the crime of controlling sports game should be a better plan, which can absorb the act of controlling game in the way of non-bribe, the act of controlling game in the way of non-material bribe, the act of football gambling after controlling game in the way of non-material bribe and the act non-gambling after controlling game. So this action of preventing football gambling may became another chance of the criminal crime development.",2010,Yong-ming,Journal of Tianjin University Science and Technology,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7532,Study on Sports Gambling Crime,"Sports gambling crime is one of specific gambling crimes, with its meaning of gaining and losing property by the results of sporting events.Criminal organizations are hierarchical agent pyramid structure, committing covertly relying on network and other technological means.Sports gambling crime in our county has profound background of social transformation and sports reform.and has characteristics such as globalization, group-oriented, intelligent, diverse and large amounts of money.In addition to its harmfulness of corrupting social values, increasing social instability and endangering financial security, sports gambling crime also destroy fair principle of sports, result in reduction of sports competition and impact on sports lottery industry.",2010,Zhang,Criminal Research,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7533,Economics of Gambling on Sports: A Multistage Stochastic Programming Approach to American Jai Alai Gambling Strategies,,2010,Zheng,Springer eBooks,10.1007/978-3-642-13205-6_11,,https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-13205-6_11,en,crossref:book-chapter | openalex:book-chapter | s2:,openalex;s2;crossref,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R7534,Study of Marketing Strategy about Sports Lottery,"This paper analyzed the extant marketing problem of sports lottery,and proposed the creative research of sports lottery marketing,such as brand effect,establish the effective excitation regulations,extent promotion methods,develop sports lottery multiple types,establish effective selling management system,set basis for the sports lottery’s long-term development.",2010,Zhu,Journal of Xinxiang University,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7535,On Historical Origin and Development of Football Gambling Activities in China,"This article reviews and analyzes the historical origins,the evolution of history and contemporary development of Football Gambling Activities in China by using iterature and logic analysis and other research methods.With a view to find ways to effectively curb the proliferation of Football Gambling Activities.This article thinks as following: China's football gambling activities have the characteristic of spread fast,wide dissemination,large gambling-related funds,a number of participants,organized gambling and many gambling methods and so on.Football gambling activities have seriously hindered the development of football,social stability,financial order stable,economical movement security and breeding corruption among officials.Football gambling activities must be resolutely banned.The effective measures to curb the rampant football gambling activities are that sports,finance and public security departments must strengthen synergies,make concerted efforts to strengthen financial supervision,squeeze cyberspace,accelerate the legislative process,reinforce warning education and insist on combining blocking and dredging.",2010,Zhu-ping,Journal of Pla Institute of Physical Education,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7536,Knowledge Management in High-Growth Companies,"This case study describes knowledge management practices in Mozzartbet, the major and fastest growing division of Stepanovic & Šipka Corporation. Mozzartbet started as sport betting business in 2001. Since then, Mozzartbet’s size has increased a few hundred times in just eight years and knowledge increase followed that pace. It can therefore be an example of knowledge management practices in high-growth companies. Technical, organizational and behavioral practices, successes and problems of knowledge management in Mozzartbet are covered, and future plans of top managers in that area are revealed. In this case study the authors describe a relaxed, academic-like organizational culture, organizational structure, strategy of development, industry and regional environment, and other internal and external factors important for knowledge management. Afterwards they present conclusions about knowledge management in Mozzartbet and future directions, according to contingency approach.Request access from your librarian to read this chapter's full text.",2010,Čudanov,IGI Global eBooks,10.4018/978-1-61692-886-5.ch014,,https://doi.org/10.4018/978-1-61692-886-5.ch014,en,openaire:Part of book or chapter of book | openalex:book-chapter | s2:,openalex;s2;openaire,3,False,False,False,,,,,
R7537,关于“海南试水博彩业”的法律思考,"新中国博彩业发展已近20年,当前博彩业的发展已出现许多始料未及的新情况和新特点。国务院发布的《关于推进海南国际旅游岛建设发展的若干意见》,将在海南试办一些国际通行的旅游体育娱乐项目,探索发展竞猜型体育彩票和大型国际赛事即开彩票。博彩业是一个特殊产业,要加强博彩业的立法研究以及政府对博彩业的法律管制,充分发挥博彩业的积极因素,避免或将不利因素降到最低。",2010,严梅,传承,,,,zh,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7538,沿海城市体育产业发展现状、问题及对策研究——以浙江省温州市为例,"通过对温州体育产业各部门资产构成、营业收入、品牌建设、从业人员、产业集群、经济效益和研发投入等情况的全面调查与分析,发现：温州体育产业企业多属中小型,并以私营企业为主,缺乏龙头企业和高质量的品牌产品,体育用品制造业、休闲健身娱乐活动业和体育用品销售业是目前温州市体育产业的主要产业部门;体育用品制造业企业从业人员学历水平低,高中级科技人员匮乏,企业R＆D经费投入不足,产品外向度较高,企业经济效益较好,产业集群化水平较低;体育用品销售业和体育彩票业发展速度较快;温州体育产业内部结构不尽合理,作为主体产业的体育服务业尤其是体育竞赛表演业尚未形成规模,对相关产业的拉动作用没有充分体现;经营管理人才存在缺口,影响企业创新能力和管理水平的提升;政府对体育产业的支持力度不够,发展环境有待进一步改善;有基础、有优势的产业部门发展缓慢。针对问题提出相应对策。",2010,吴宝升,Acta Scientiarum Naturalium Universitatis Sunyatseni,,,,zh,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7539,中国足彩走向何方——合理疏导 更有效的改进规则,国家发行足球彩票，已经六年多了，目睹当今之现状，总想写点文字，表达一下自已的观点和感受。 当初，中国足球彩票的发行是适时的，在胜负彩票发行初期，有识之士已经认识到这是在给中国博彩做嫁衣。足彩发行的初期，每期胜负彩票销量可以高达两亿，现在每期胜负彩票销量包括任9场在内也不过三千多万，这是一个不容否认的事实!应该引起重视了!,2010,周莲爱,彩票研究,,,,zh,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7540,中国足坛“假、赌、黑”三大顽症的主要成因及遏制策略,采用文献资料法、逻辑分析法深入探究中国足坛“假球、赌球、黑哨”三大顽症滋生的主要成因，并据此提出针对性的干预措施和遏制策略。认为经济利益驱使、核心价值观迷失、管理部门定位不清、相关法律法规不健全以及人性的深层需求影响造成了“假球、赌球、黑哨”三大顽症滋生。为消除这一现象，应当破解足球俱乐部的生存困境，重建足球从业群体的核心价值观，重新定位足协角色，建立反赌监控机构和常态监管机制，尝试将体育博彩业公开化、有限合法化和适度开放，应积极借鉴国外打击“假球、赌球、黑哨”的经验。,2010,张磊,河北体育学院学报,,,,zh,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7541,体育彩票“排列三”的研究,体育彩票“排列三”每期出三个数字，知道其中的概率规律，就能帮助彩票购买人提高中彩收益。本文基于对历史数据的统计处理分析，从和值、和尾、跨度等方面对“排列三”的长短期规律进行分析，建立模型，可以比较准确的预测。,2010,李秀明,魅力中国,,,,ja,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7542,体育彩票“排列三”有关问题的研究,,2010,杨琛,科技资讯,,,,zh,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R7543,媒介使用與媒介依賴對運動博弈資訊可信度的影響－電視、報紙、網路的比較,"The purposes of this study were to investigate the influence of audiences' media use and dependency on sports lottery information on the information credibility, making the comparison of television, newspaper and Internet. Meanwhile, by examining the ”relative credibility” as well as the ”absolute credibility” among the three media, the study aim to provide some suggestion for the researchers and the information producers in the future. The study collected data by conducting a Internet survey with the questionnaire, obtaining 267 samples in total. The conclusions of the study were as follows: 1. Among the three media, sports lottery information on the Internet got the highest ranking in its relative credibility, following ones are that on television and newspapers. However, in terms of the absolute credibility, the distances of the three were closer despite of the fact that the ranking was the same. 2. As for the source credibility, the professional sports commentaries obtained the higher credibility in the traditional media including television and newspaper, while the normal fans and famous bloggers gained the higher credibility on the Internet. 3. Among the demographic variables, only genders and educational levels could partly predict the credibility of sports lottery information in media. 4. In all the three cases, the media dependency variable were the better predictors of the credibility than the media use ones, which supports the hypothesis of this study.",2010,王皓昀,,10.29595/zhwhgx.201008.0006,,https://doi.org/10.29595/zhwhgx.201008.0006,zh,openalex:article | s2:Review,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R7544,喜迎“桥牌进社区”一周年——记武汉市硚口区集贤社区桥牌活动基地,金秋十月，我们迎来了中国桥牌协会授予的、中国体育彩票公积金受助的武汉市斫口区集贤社区桥牌活动基地创建一周年的日子。一年来，在各级桥牌协会的关心下，在市老干部局和区委、区政府领导的支持下，该活动点的桥牌活动开展得红红火火。从当初几十人每次两三桌人打桥牌，发展到一百多人二十余桌。武汉晚报、老年文汇报、市电视台先后多次报道活动基地的事迹，受到社区广大居民的称赞，也引起省、市体育局、老干部局和老年委的高度重视。,2010,甘德润,桥牌,,,,zh,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
