R8079,Research on the Application of SDC State Analysis in the Study of Public Awareness of Sport Lottery Ticket and Purchase Psychology,"Sport lottery ticket income can contribute greatly to the development of sports in China.Adopted SDC state analysis,this research conducted a profound and extensive the study on the random data collected from ten cities such as Beijing,Shanghai.The results indicated that the public generally has an inadequate understanding of sport lottery ticket and that the main reason to buy the ticket is to win a prize.Therefore,a moderate number of winning prizes may increase its sale.And the promoting of its significance and popularizing of its theoretical knowledge can also help sustain a wholesale development of the sport lottery ticket market in China.",2005,Zhang,,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R8080,THOUGHTS ON DEVELOPMENT OF SPORT GAMBLING IN CHINA,"AbstrcatIn the past ten years,sport gambling developed quickly and played a more and more important role in sports industry. Adopting the methods of investigation,documentation,the paper makes a objective analysis on existing problems and causes in the development of sports gambling and . developmental trend of the sports gambling in China ,and some countermeasures are given on existing problems in the development of sports gambling ,which providing reference to steady development of sport gambling industry in China.",2005,Zhang,Journal of Anhui Normal University,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R8081,The influences of soccer gambling on modern competitive sports and the related countermeasures,"Gambling,a kind of social hazard, has been involved in the sports field especially in the field of soccer, and will bring in dangerous results to the development of soccer and the competitive sports career.By analyzing the soccer gambling present situation in China,this article pointed out that it had an hazard influence on society and competitive sports.As well,the article put forward some countermeasures.",2005,Zhi-ping,journal of physical education,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
