R8423,The February Lull in sport - Sports Gambling,"Late February and early March on the sport's scene is a time between, and a time of anticipation. This is especially true if you live in the cold climates, where by this time of year cabin fever has set in, the Super Bowl is over, and the sports in season are biding their time.",1992,Crepeau,Journal of International Crisis and Risk Communication Research,,,,en,openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2,2,False,False,False,,,,,
R8424,Gambling on sport: Policy issues.,"The most significant public policy issue associated with sports betting is legalization. Supporters of legalization rest the bulk of their case on the economic benefits the state can experience. They also assert that legalization will have a major negative impact on the extent of illegal gambling. Those who are against further legalization, particularly amateur and professional sports leagues, the horse race industry, and legal bookmakers, point out that sports wagering is not very profitable and is very risky for the operator. Furthermore, legal wagering will be unable to compete effectively with the price of illegal operations. It is highly likely that the recently introduced federal legislation, S.474, Professional and Amateur Sports Protection Act, prohibiting further legalization of sports betting will be enacted.",1992,Frey,Journal of gambling studies,10.1007/bf01024122,24242018,https://doi.org/10.1007/bf01024122,eng,crossref:journal-article | europepmc:Journal Article|src=MED | openaire:Article | openalex:article | pubmed:Journal Article | s2:JournalArticle,pubmed;europepmc;openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,6,False,False,False,,,,,
R8425,Pricing inefficiencies in the football-betting market,"Since Pankoff (Journal of Business, 1968), investment writers have recognized that bets on the outcome of football games provide an unusually direct test of pricing efficiency by market consensus. In a football context, prices are proxied by pointspreads (values ranging from 1 to 50+, which represent the bettors' expectations regarding the stronger team's victory margin). Efficiency refers to the impossibility of using betting rules based on past performance or information not discounted by the spread to win consistently.",1992,Kochman,Atlantic Economic Journal,10.1007/bf02300185,,https://doi.org/10.1007/bf02300185,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R8426,Book Review of super bookie: Inside Las Vegas sports gambling,,1992,Smith,Journal of Gambling Studies,10.1007/bf01014656,,https://doi.org/10.1007/bf01014656,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:book-review | s2:Review,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
R8427,Sucker bet or sure thing: A critical analysis of sports lotteries.,"A paradox currently exists regarding legal sports gambling in North America: various forms are flourishing in Nevada, Oregon, and several Canadian provinces, while at the same time the United States Congress is conducting hearings on two bills that would prohibit any new state-sponsored sports gambling initiatives. This study examines the issue of why some jurisdictions are enthusiastic about legal sports gambling while others strongly resist the concept. In reviewing these divergent viewpoints, a case study of the newfledged Canadian ""Sport Select"" gambling format is presented. This example is used to highly the perils and payoffs of a typical state-sponsored sports gambling scheme, with a view toward broadening our understanding of how they work and how they might be fairer to the public.",1992,Smith,Journal of gambling studies,10.1007/bf01024121,24242017,https://doi.org/10.1007/bf01024121,eng,crossref:journal-article | europepmc:Journal Article|src=MED | openaire:Article | openalex:article | pubmed:Journal Article | s2:JournalArticle;Review,pubmed;europepmc;openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,6,False,False,False,,,,,
R8428,足球彩票“火”京城,"1992年6月26日上午9时,东四先锋体育用品商社前人头攒动,一条长龙排出几十米开外,马路上的自行车道成了自行车存放处,一位市民感慨道:有好几年没见过排这么长的队了。原来,人们在抢购紧俏商品一张薄薄的纸——足球彩票。排在长龙第一位的中年人是早上5点来的。球迷们似乎害怕300万张足球彩票会被一抢而光,一个个争先恐后,小小的柜台几次被挤翻,几名身强力壮的警察在现场维持秩序也无济于事。先锋体育用品商社",1992,Zhang,体育博览,,,,ja,openalex_non_en:article,openalex_non_en,1,False,False,False,,,,,
R8429,The degree of inefficiency in the football betting market Statistical tests,"Abstract This paper tests the hypothesis that the football betting market is efficient. Our statistical tests are stronger than those in previous studies, and we examine both NFL and college data over a sample period of fifteen years. Our statistical tests detect two specific biases in the NFL market and an unspecified bias in the college market. We examine the year-to-year consistency and magnitudes of the biases and find that the NFL bias against home teams has been nearly eliminated, while the bias against underdogs has increased. Profitable exploitation of the biases depends upon transaction costs.",1991,Golec,Journal of Financial Economics,10.1016/0304-405x(91)90034-h,,https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-405x(91)90034-h,en,crossref:journal-article | openaire:Article | openalex:article | s2:,openalex;s2;crossref;openaire,4,False,False,False,,,,,
